/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-07T20:59:31-08:00","id":1467152,"title":"","content":"I Have No Cash, and I Must Scream<br /> <br /> Looking forward to what Kindred partying is all about.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-07T22:19:03-08:00","id":1467154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1467058-sin-again-daeva-now-available-on-storytellers-vault-2e-requiem-clan-book?p=1467152#post1467152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I Have No Cash, and I Must Scream<br /> <br /> Looking forward to what Kindred partying is all about.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don\u2019t worry, the book will be waiting for you! The Daeva love a big crowd, even if they have to wait\u2026.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-08T12:04:06-08:00","id":1467190,"title":"","content":"Alright, time for our first excerpt and commentary!<br /> <br /> The Star-Crossed are one of two new bloodlines in the book, with the power to put humans in bizarre biological time loops and then bleed them for a golden sap that can produce a whole cavalcade of strange, time-defying effects, As noted above, they're probably my favourite of the pair, though only just. I'm a big fan of bloodlines that are, to put it crudely, evil bastards. When you look past the self-pity and aesthetics, the Star-Crossed are<i> monstrous,</i> but in a way that I think can be compelling for players and Storytellers alike. Not everyone will want to go there, but I like my bloodlines morally thorny, and the Custodians are covered in vines.<br /> <br /> <i>Conceptually</i>, the Star-Crossed didn't change much through drafts, though we tinkered a lot with their mechanics. They always had their Purities, but creating them originally involved a Devotion rather than an inherent power. In development, it occurred to me that we didn't really need the roadblock of going out and buying a power, so their Purification power became something they can just <i>do</i>. That's a frequent theme in my theory of game design: let players do the thing.<br /> <br /> Now, those of you who've read <b>Night Horrors: Spilled Blood</b> are probably wondering what the connection to the Everlasting is. Originally? None. The author hadn't read them! At first, I worried the concept was too close to the Everlasting, but the more I thought about it, the more I liked the coincidence, and we decided it was more interesting to lean into it than to abandon it. That's how we developed the idea of them having a weird substance to harvest. The first draft of the Star-Crossed was a fun idea, but it lacked a bit of player utility, so I wanted to give them something they could justify their existence to the rest of the All Night Society. Electrum and Ichor work very differently, but there's enough overlap to make you wonder. We also included a rumor to suggest some possible conflicts and/or connections, and I tweaked their Discipline spread to match the four the Everlasting have access to (they originally had Vigor, but, apart from symmetry with the Everlasting, Resilience felt more appropriate anyway).<br /> <br /> One last detail that's just kind of funny: the &quot;Once upon a midnight darkly...&quot; entry for the bloodline was originally the Erzs\u00e9bet's, and the Erzs\u00e9bet's was originally the Star-Crossed's. However, the Custodian's mirror bane and general vibe were just too perfect not to reference Dorian Grey, and the Cavaliers already have Elizabeth Bathory as a possible founder, so I felt it was better not to overload their origins with references. So, the Star-Crossed author and I traded, and I think both bloodlines are the better for it.<br /> <br /> Anyhow, here's the Star-Crossed. Tomorrow, I'll be back with the other new bloodline, the Moda Mortale...<br /> <br /> <b>Star-Crossed: The ones who covet you</b><br /> <br /> &quot;Time is a river; I am the dam.&quot;<br /> <br /> <i>Photos were insufficient to capture his beauty, or the grace with which he moved upon the dance floor. Yet the years peeled him back in layers, reducing him to a rotten husk. Eventually, the neighbors complained about the smell, and then the law came knocking. I fought like a demon to prevent them from taking away what was left of my love, but they buried him where I could never find him.<br /> <br /> In retrospect, I understand why my sire chose me, even if she came to regret it; I was halfway Star-Crossed already. Crossed in a few ways, really.<br /> <br /> Even in the Requiem, all I really wanted was him. I took to the streets looking for someone I could mold into his image, but the nights slid by in a rabid need that no amount of blood could slake. If I couldn\u2019t have him, I would sooner tear out my own eyes than look upon another.<br /> <br /> So I did. Now I hunt by touch and sound alone, but I\u2019ve managed to find three facsimiles. It takes some getting used to, all their weeping, but I just turn up the gramophone and wait for them \u2014 some night \u2014 to take up my offer to dance.<br /> <br /> Ah, to love again.</i><br /> <br /> Eternity is empty without devotion. And yet, most Daeva wile away their nights avoiding it, all for fear of getting caught on mortal lives the same way they slip hooks through their victims. Not all Serpents are willing to give up on happily ever after, but it\u2019s the ever part that\u2019s elusive. Their blood aches for humanity, yet humanity is fragile. The flesh wanes; the mind fades. Time is the enemy of perfection, and for every vampire who thinks she\u2019s found true, eternal love, another is laying his soulmate to rest for the third time this century. The Embrace is no solution. Death sours relationships and adds another predator to the pack. Ghouls? Slavery isn\u2019t love, and addiction is just another layer of removal.<br /> <br /> But the Star-Crossed aren\u2019t content to give up on human affection; it\u2019s the one thing in the Requiem they find worthy of possession or preservation. To keep their own despair at bay, the Custodians entrap kine who embody qualities they most admire or lust for, imprisoning them in bizarre time loops so they can bask in a captive\u2019s unchanging state. Night after night they maintain this stasis, spending precious Vitae to ensure their \u201cPurities\u201d remain uncorrupted. Kept pristine long enough, these time-trapped bodies transmute their blood into a strange substance the Star-Crossed calls Electrum, after the amber tears of the Heliades, who eternally mourned the death of their brother Pha\u00ebthon, child of the Sun. Some (most) Custodians tap their Purities \u2014 <i>oh </i>so carefully \u2014 for this golden sap, bestowing its gifts on any who would consume it. Many Kindred would pay a pretty price for a vial.<br /> <br /> However, as much as they would wish it otherwise, nothing lasts forever. Sooner or later, a Custodian can\u2019t keep up the maintenance, or her Purity escapes, or she befouls him with her Vitae. Then, all that lost time catches up with a vengeance, reducing the poor mortal to a wasted corpse.<br /> <br /> This loss pushes the Star-Crossed to self-destruction. The loathing that consumes them is as low as their euphoric obsession was high. Therefore, they find outlets for these emotional storms. Like Pygmalion, they craft their ideal in marble, or paint canvas after canvas to capture each coveted feature. Others hunt for a replacement among humanity\u2019s ranks, and while they might never find a true doppelg\u00e4nger, if the eyes are right on one, and the mouth on another\u2026 the parts might all add up to a perfect whole. For the Star-Crossed, solace can only be found in the spaces between life and death, where corruption halts and the night stands still.<br /> <br /> <b>Why you want to be us</b><br /> <br /> You need not taint those you would pluck from Death\u2019s greedy hands: We can show you how to make them into undying angels. Forsake the fruitless lust of other Serpents; it leads to nothing but despair. Instead, we\u2019ll cup your hands around the most precious embers, fan them to blazing brightness, and then you \u2014 and you alone \u2014 will have been witness to a moment of true perfection.<br /> <br /> <b>Why you should fear us</b><br /> <br /> Why do you keep trying to leave? There\u2019s nowhere on earth where our love won\u2019t lead us back to you. We would never stoop to polluting you as thralls, or pass on our Damnation. In our grasp, you\u2019ll always be pristine, incorruptible against the ravages of time. You cannot wish to rot! What, you want to return to your \u201cfamily?\u201d No, we shall not let them tarnish your perfection. Don\u2019t weep in your gilded prison, precious one. Freedom is a price worth paying for eternity.<br /> <br /> <b>Why we should fear ourselves</b><br /> <br /> Whatever moron said, \u201cIf you love someone, let them go,\u201d didn\u2019t have to face fucking forever alone. We cling to our Purities or else our hearts become little more than deadweight. Without someone to safeguard and hold dear, we\u2019re forced to confront the wretched things we\u2019ve become in the name of love, losing ourselves in the purposeless depths.<br /> <br /> <b>Parent Clan: </b>Daeva<br /> <br /> <b>Nicknames:</b> Custodians, Sophists (disrespectful)<br /> <br /> <b>Bloodline Bane (The Curse of Self-Reflection):</b> A Star-Crossed obsesses outwardly to avoid the awful thing time warps her soul into. The closer she is to the Beast, the more visual representations of a Custodian resemble a monstrous, distorted parody of her form. If a mortal sees a facsimile of the vampire (in a mirror, a photo, a video, a drawing, etc.), [REDACTED].<br /> <br /> <b>Disciplines: </b>Celerity, <i>Dominate</i>, <i>Majesty</i>, Resilience<br /> <br /> <b>Bloodline Origins (Excerpt)</b><br /> <br /> Once upon a midnight darkly, a beautiful young lord wished to age no more. Instead, his prized portrait would accept the burdens of flesh from his charmed shoulders, reflecting all his sins as he took his fill of life\u2019s pleasures. The man ravaged the world, and in turn the world ravaged his painting. After many years and many depravities, smiling faces wronged in the lord\u2019s past returned to haunt him, though whether they were truth or delusion is unknown. Nonetheless, he gave commands, and all smiles stopped together. He would hold against his past and future to protect his obsessions, even if it meant defying Time itself. So, the lord resolved to destroy the only true evidence of his crimes. He wallows in its remains still, a husk among the fragments of a ruined masterpiece \u2014 deliriously ever after.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":192,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","user":"Yossarian","date":". 11-08-2021, 04:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-08T15:40:04-08:00","id":1467203,"title":"","content":"I think I found just the bloodline I needed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-08T16:29:15-08:00","id":1467205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1467058-sin-again-daeva-now-available-on-storytellers-vault-2e-requiem-clan-book?p=1467203#post1467203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think I found just the bloodline I needed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Star-Crossed elders are...hmm. I don't know how to express the feeling outside of existentially terrified screaming.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-08T18:51:04-08:00","id":1467217,"title":"","content":"I picked it up as soon as I saw this post! I haven't finished reading it yet, but so far it looks extremely promising.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27139-chevaliermalfet","name":"ChevalierMalFet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-08T19:31:58-08:00","id":1467222,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1467058-sin-again-daeva-now-available-on-storytellers-vault-2e-requiem-clan-book?p=1467205#post1467205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Star-Crossed elders are...hmm. I don't know how to express the feeling outside of existentially terrified screaming.</div> </div> </div> </div>One of my players specifically loves to have the character locked in a... &quot;complicated&quot;... relationship. The PCs are humans, at first.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-09T13:12:18-08:00","id":1467286,"title":"","content":"Alright, let's do our second new bloodline!<br /> <br /> Like the Star-Crossed, the Moda Mortale (&quot;the deadly fashion&quot;) were conceptually pretty solid upon first draft. They're Daeva who play at being fashion icons (models, designers, etc.), but who secretly spread violent messages via the Cacophony, using their &quot;official&quot; jobs as cover. That mostly was there in the first draft, though originally they had an element of erasing their victims from public consciousness, which was <i>really </i>cool, but didn't quite fit narratively with them making statements through their killing. They also didn't have Protean, but I thought that would be an interesting twist on their being assassins and fashion icons. They can use their shapeshifting in non-obvious ways, mutating their bodies into weird, transhumanist forms for their runway walks, but also grow massive claws when they gut you over drinks later. They have what I think is one of the most interesting Discipline spreads in the book; I don't <i>think </i>there are any bloodlines with Obfuscate, Protean, <i>and </i>Majesty.<br /> <br /> This is another bloodline I really like not only for really embracing its high concept, but for being pretty damn antagonistic. They're definitely playable, but I think a lot of fun comes from using them as rather frightening antagonists: bizarre, mutative assassins who can make you love them in one moment, and disappear from sight the next. I also really like the little mystery of their origins that the author seeded through the piece, especially what's really going on with their purported founder. I suspect Ginevra will return in future books...<br /> <br /> Also, on a personal note, I'm just really pleased with how the fake newspaper scrap in their intro ended up looking. Layout can be kind of a thankless task, and that was fun to put together. On a side note, the except below will seem to cut off; it's intentional, but makes more sense with the proper formatting in the book.<br /> <br /> Anyway, here's the Moda Mortale, in all their glory. Tomorrow we'll be looking at one of the updated bloodlines: The Children of Judas. And <i>oh boy </i>do I have a lot to say about them.<br /> <br /> <b>Moda Mortale: The ones who cut you out</b><br /> <br /> &quot;Watch yourself, honey: I'm dressed to kill.&quot;<br /> <br /> <b><i>Mob lawyer hung from office window</i></b><br /> <br /> <i>On Monday morning, a grisly scene greeted Seventh Avenue at Main Street, where defense attorney Blake Chilton\u2019s remains were found on display at his former law firm. The cryptic phrase \u201cBANG BANG\u201d was emblazoned in seven-foot-high letters on the building\u2019s exterior windows on the 27th floor, in what the authorities have confirmed was Mr. Chilton\u2019s own blood. Police would not comment further on the message or its significance, and no firearm use was in evidence. Witnesses placed Mr. Chilton the night before at La Verit\u00e0 Italian Cuisine in the fashionable East End District around 7 p.m. He was last seen dining with an unidentified woman in her early- to mid-20s; she is considered a person of interest.<br /> <br /> Over the past year, Mr. Chilton made a name for himself after a legal career of relative obscurity, representing high-profile clients with ties to organized crime, notably at the controversial trial and subsequent acquittal of Sigismund \u201cZiggy\u201d Carmichael, an alleged capo of Arturo Sangiovanni.<br /> <br /> This marks the third assassination of a high-profile criminal attorney in as many months, and Metro PD is calling these homicides \u201cprofessional.\u201d The perpetrator or perpetrators\u2019 methods share little in common, aside from their theatricality, with a daring, grotesque display at each crime scene. Police are</i><br /> <br /> In the vicious world of Kindred politics, sometimes you want a rival to disappear quietly \u2014 and sometimes, you want to send a message. For the latter, you need a killer with a keen sense of style. Of panache. In other words, you need the Moda Mortale.<br /> <br /> The Fashionistas are where style meets substance in the All Night Society. From poisoning to strangulation, sniper\u2019s scope to pistol whip, they\u2019ve mastered the assassin\u2019s handbook, and they\u2019re as chic as they are deadly. You\u2019ll see them coming because they want you to, in stiletto heels crafted from actual stilettos and Protean-perfect feather coifs. The couture angle isn\u2019t just aesthetics, though. They really are models and designers, and they\u2019re on the bleeding edge of fashion in a way few among the dead could ever hope to achieve. Some are even renowned beyond the Danse Macabre, voguing across the edge of the Masquerade.<br /> <br /> Ironically, most Kindred don\u2019t realize they\u2019re anything but a bunch of fashionable Daeva, or that they\u2019re a bloodline at all. For the Moda Mortale, covert means overt, using their \u201cday jobs\u201d as cover to travel between high-end events that just happen to coincide with a nasty murder or two. Kindred or kine, sire or childe, it\u2019s all the same to these Widows, just so long as the check clears. But you\u2019re not just paying to solve a problem: You\u2019re paying for publicity. More than mere murderers, the Moda Mortale operate the Cacophony like a sewing machine, stitching in bloody messages the All Night Society can\u2019t rip out.<br /> <br /> An alderman dies in bed with his mistress, rose petals scattered around the bed; the Carthians cancel their plans for the dockyard. A research scientist takes a bullet through the head, but a knife defiles his corpse with the words Taking Note; the Kogaion flees town. A prominent occultist is crucified on the eve of the summer solstice, on the highest skyscraper in the city; the Mother\u2019s Army declares war.<br /> <br /> Are there easier ways to send a message? Sure, if you\u2019ve got no taste. But if you had a simple message, you wouldn\u2019t come to the Moda Mortale. Each death is a two-pronged solution, one that destroys whoever happens to be standing in the way of a client\u2019s scheme and fosters an environment to further that plan. All without a paper trail \u2014 not the bad kind, at any rate. The Widows ensure you always make the headlines. Sometimes that means a little character assassination before the knives come out, destroying the victim\u2019s social life in preparation for the \u201cmoral\u201d they\u2019ll be sending the Kindred. For the Widows, this is the ultimate edit. And fashion is all about editing.<br /> <br /> The bloodline\u2019s services are available only to the true elites of the All Night Society, yet to these upper echelons, the Moda Mortale are a complicated problem. Killing is just as much a crime among the dead as the living, though one might ask when moral and legal quandaries have ever really troubled the Damned. More troubling are rumors of Widows devouring their own when they fail their high-stakes missions, but surely a bloodline of assassins built around ritual diablerie couldn\u2019t have been so\u2026 successful? Surely.<br /> <br /> <b>Why you want to be us</b><br /> <br /> When you send someone across the final threshold, the least you can do is dress for the occasion, and we\u2019ll reshape you into a couture killing machine. Joining us is getting on the Kindred A List, and isn\u2019t it better to be part of the club than at the mercy of the hunt?<br /> <br /> <b>Why you should fear us</b><br /> <br /> There\u2019s death and then there\u2019s death. The former is casting off your daylight life like last season\u2019s furs; the latter is getting on the wrong side of our blades. Don\u2019t worry, doll, we\u2019ll make sure your end is unforgettable. They just won\u2019t be talking about you.<br /> <br /> <b>Why we should fear ourselves</b><br /> <br /> Being perfect takes constant rigor and endless competition. Look over your shoulder because the next bitch is coming up the ranks; how long before she makes you obsolete? Letting yourself be outshone, outmatched, outdated \u2014 that\u2019s career suicide. And if you don\u2019t work for us, you get the bad edit. So take a long, hard look in the mirror. Are you as good as you were yesterday? That\u2019s not good enough. You\u2019ve got to be fucking better. No sympathy for even the smallest glimpse of weakness in our ranks. One slip, and you\u2019ll plummet into last season. Forever.<br /> <br /> <b>Parent Clan:</b> Daeva<br /> <br /> <b>Nicknames:</b> Fashionistas, Widows (among those in the know)<br /> <br /> <b>Bloodline Bane (The Impeccable Curse):</b> The Widows are obsessed with perfection. While this makes them fastidious killers and fashion icons, it also means that if something disrupts their work, their manicured Requiems may crack. When a Fashionista suffers a setback or finds a flaw in her current plans (such as fulfilling an Aspiration), her player must roll Humanity. On a failure, [REDACTED].<br /> <br /> <b>Disciplines: </b><i>Majesty</i>, Obfuscate, <i>Protean</i>, Vigor<br /> <br /> <b>New Merit: Medium Is Message (\u2022 or \u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <br /> <b>Prerequisites: </b>Moda Mortale Status \u2022<br /> <br /> <b>Effect:</b> When your character kills, the precise meaning and intent of the death will be clear to all Kindred, even those without any Cacophony Savvy. At one dot, roll Wits + Crafts/Expression to create a perfect crime scene, using whichever Skill would apply best to the message. At two dots, she can choose to make her message sensible only to intended recipients. Any attempt to decipher the meaning only succeeds with an exceptional success, and only after suffering a penalty equal to your character\u2019s Crafts or Expression dots, whichever applied to the crime scene.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-10T12:40:22-08:00","id":1467372,"title":"","content":"Welcome back to another episode of Yossarian rambles about Draculas!<br /> <br /> Yesterday I promised I'd talk about the Children of Judas, who I <i>think </i>might be my favourite bloodline in the book. That was an unexpected outcome, as they were easily the bloodline I've liked the least of anything we've updated.<br /> <br /> So, a little preamble: The original Suicide Kings entry took that name very literally. They made people commit suicide, and the book included a detailed list of the kinds of suicide one could inflict on people.<br /> <br /> Suffice it to say, it was rough. There's a lot I could say about the old version, but I prefer to be positive in these posts, and I think whatever criticisms I have of it are pretty self-evident. You can have a look for yourselves, but be warned, it's not pretty. It's trying to do something it's wholly not equipped to do, and the results are very frustrating.<br /> <br /> <i>All that said</i>, it wasn't unsalvageable. There were some interesting concepts, and the lore had a lot of cool plot seeds I thought we could take in fun directions. I hemmed and hawed a lot about including this bloodline at all, but I ultimately convinced myself when I decided the original write-up was a hit job. It's what the rest of the All Night Society says about the bloodline: that they can make you kill yourself! That they're <i>obsessed </i>with suicide!<br /> <br /> Starting with that basic concept, that the CoJ suffer from bad press, the author decided the Hanged are actually addicted to grief and regret, not suicide. And who goes around with tons of that sort of baggage? The Kindred. Instead of &quot;forcing people to commit suicide&quot;, it's a (rare) side effect of their desire to punish the wicked and feed on their lust for grief. Does this make them good guys? Big nope. They don't care if what they do is righteous; just that they get their awful fix. This kept the thorny morality I like so much (as noted above), but turned it into something that didn't feel icky. We also wanted to keep the idea that the bloodline sometimes arises spontaneously from suicide victims, which does hold to some older myths, and helps explain why they've survived so long. It also gave the Dolorae sisters (their purported founders) more to do, and you can see that thread move through each of the rumors.<br /> <br /> Aside from reframing the bloodline's goals and methods, we also made some pretty big changes to their Disciplines and bane. Despond definitely wasn't going to make it into our update as a Discipline, but Nightmare slotted in very nicely. We also felt that Auspex still fit, due to their desire to seek out sins...but that left us with a quandary. The original CoJ had Auspex, Despond, Majesty, and Resilience -- three &quot;special&quot; Disciplines and only one of the Daeva clan Disciplines. I've mentioned before that my preference is to not have bloodlines with more than two special powers, and to almost <i>never </i>lose their signature power...but, here, I was persuaded otherwise. The author made a good argument that this bloodline is the &quot;through a mirror darkly&quot; of the Daeva. They still make you spill your guts, but <i>not </i>because you love them.<br /> <br /> As for the bane, it actually isn't too different from the original, at least thematically, but it manifests (as Daeva banes often do) in feeding. In first edition, the CoJ lost Willpower for not &quot;exploring&quot; a victim's pain; now they need to feed on it. This isn't helped by the fact that the bloodline's &quot;gift&quot; of terrible visions only manifests when they drink from people they've fed from only once. They are still Serpents, after all. They're just addicted to a different aspect of you.<br /> <br /> While these new Children of Judas are a lot less focused on suicide than the originals, that theme is still there. Because of that, it's not a bloodline you should bring into your game lightly. We talk about safety measures in Chapter Three of the book, but I think it bears repeating: if this bloodline's presence would upset players, please don't use them. I think there are interesting stories to be told with them, but not everyone will be in for them.<br /> <br /> Anyway, here's the Children of Judas. Tomorrow, I'll be back with the Nelapsi.<br /> <br /> <b>Children of Judas: The ones who eat your grief.</b><br /> <br /> &quot;Think about what you've done.&quot;<br /> <br /> First thing\u2019s first: We didn\u2019t name ourselves. Who the fuck would want to be called <i>the Children of Judas</i>? That name\u2019s nothing but baggage, and we\u2019ve got more than enough of that already. Unfortunately, we also have all the internal organization of an orgy for the blind, so we\u2019re stuck with it.<br /> <br /> Second, we didn\u2019t ask to be this way. Ours isn\u2019t the sort of illustrious lineage you join in search of wealth and prestige. Every single one of us is a victim, of one kind or another, and that\u2019s before the rest of the dead-man-walking crowd starts taking swings. Probably why \u201cHanged\u201d is our preferred sobriquet. We\u2019re cheery like that.<br /> <br /> For a bunch of killjoy grief-addicts that nobody wants at their party, we\u2019ve been around awhile. You can find records of us in all sorts of domains going back centuries. They\u2019re usually records of execution, but hey. It\u2019s good to have a history. Of course, that isn\u2019t the same as knowing where we come from, but we\u2019ll get to that. Where we\u2019ve been isn\u2019t as important as what we do.<br /> <br /> We taste things in the blood. Tragedy, sin, remorse, whatever you want to call it. If you\u2019ve been naughty and we take a nip, we get a peek at your shame. Yes, it happens every time; no, we can\u2019t stop it. Wish it weren\u2019t so. Worse, we <i>need </i>those terrible, no good memories \u2014 need them almost as much as we need the Blood.<br /> <br /> Picture a junkie. The most strung-out, hollow-eyed meth addict who ever pissed on a bus stop at 4AM on December 31st. That\u2019s us, except instead of black tar and bricks, we\u2019re craving your worst betrayals and most painful, secret failures, dredging them up from the bleakest annals of your mind in living color. Sure, any Serpent can make you spill your guts with a pout and a wiggle, but we make you feel bad about it. We can\u2019t make you feel squat about <i>us</i>, but we can make you feel really, really terrible about yourself. Easy to see why we\u2019re so popular.<br /> <br /> Last thing: That oh-so-jolly nickname the rest of the no-pulse crowd slapped on us? Really overblown. It\u2019s not as if we go around handing out cyanide and razor blades like Halloween candy. But\u2026 we\u2019re addicts. Desperate ones. And you know who\u2019s got just oodles of tasty atrocities squirreled away? Vampires, especially old ones. Apparently, when faced with several hundred years\u2019 worth of remorse all at once, of suddenly caring about all the lives they\u2019ve casually razed, some of our \u201cdonors\u201d off themselves rather than experience one more moment of their rotten Requiems. That sort of thing tends to cause a stir, especially when it\u2019s a prince or some other highly-visible asshole who decides to give themself a tan. Doesn\u2019t matter it\u2019s only happened, like, ten times in all of recorded history. A couple dozen at most. Accidentally cause a few horrid old leeches to dust themselves, and all of a sudden you\u2019re the Suicide Kings.<br /> <br /> Fucking great.<br /> <br /> <b>Why you want to be us</b><br /> <br /> It\u2019s a nasty burden to yearn for people\u2019s worst crimes and regrets, and no one\u2019s going to thank you for bringing that shit up. Still, there\u2019s a poetry in what we do. In what we are. We\u2019re consequences for those who face none, a conscience for monsters who\u2019ve discarded their own. It\u2019s almost worth being treated like a cross between a leper and the worst kind of snitch. Almost.<br /> <br /> <b>Why you should fear us</b><br /> <br /> We know what you did. We know where all the bodies are buried, and we can count the exact number of ribs on each skeleton stuffed in your closet. Your worst choices are our best meals, but we need you to feel the guilt again to fill our bellies. It\u2019s okay if you don\u2019t remember how. We shall remind you.<br /> <br /> <b>Why we should fear ourselves</b><br /> <br /> We show people the worst of themselves and lap up their tears like bloody gumdrops. It earns us exactly zero friends, a truly staggering amount of hate, and we can\u2019t. Fucking. Stop. The only way to end our addiction to misery is to end ourselves, and if that isn\u2019t some razor-sharp irony, nothing is.<br /> <br /> <b>Parent Clan: </b>Daeva<br /> <br /> <b>Nicknames: </b>The Hanged (among themselves), Suicide Kings (among others)<br /> <br /> Bloodline Bane (The Grievous Curse): The Children of Judas are addicted to the blood of people exper*iencing grief, remorse, or regret. This goes beyond the drive to feed that all Kindred experience, as even Hanged full of Vitae still feel the need to taste misery on their fangs. If a Suicide King goes more than (Humanity) nights without consuming Vitae from one or more characters experiencing sorrowful emotions [REDACTED].<br /> <br /> <b>Disciplines: </b><i>Auspex</i>, Celerity, <i>Nightmare</i>, Vigor<br /> <br /> <b>Bloodline Origins (Excerpt)</b><br /> <br /> Once upon a midnight darkly, there was a maiden locked in a tower surrounded by a deep, dark wood. Many a young man rode forth to rescue her, yet none survived, for one by one, the forest claimed them all. The maiden lamented their terrible fates, but eventually she could bear no more. She hung herself with her golden hair \u2014 grown long and thick in captivity \u2014 so that no more fools would throw away their precious lives. Soon after, however, a gallant knight finally conquered the perils of the wood, arriving at the tower only to find the maiden pale with death. Overcome, he wept for her, and when his tears fell upon her cold flesh, she awoke with a terrible thirst. She drank from the knight, first his tears, then his blood, then his life. Now she hides from the world in dark caves and dungeon keeps, or even atop the tallest mountain peaks, but no matter how treacherous the path, a brave champion will always reach her haven\u2026 and then she\u2019ll drink him too \u2014 miserably ever after.<br /> <br /> <b>Bloodline Gift: A Taste of Grief</b><br /> <br /> The Hanged would argue over their innate ability being called a \u201cgift,\u201d but they can\u2019t deny it feeds their sorrowful addiction.<br /> <br /> When a Child of Judas feeds from a vessel for the first time, she receives a brief vision of a tragic event from that person\u2019s past. The vampire has no control over what she sees, but it\u2019s almost always something the subject experienced a breaking point over; particularly young or innocent victims might, therefore, provide no vision at all.<br /> <br /> The information provided by this gift may or may not be useful on its own, as these visions are rarely clear, but the insight can often guide the use of a Suicide King\u2019s Despond Devotions.<br /> <br /> This ability cannot be suppressed.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":192,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","user":"Yossarian","date":". 11-10-2021, 03:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-11T13:06:43-08:00","id":1467468,"title":"","content":"Welcome back to our...several...part series. Today, let's turn to the Nelapsi.<br /> <br /> Unlike the Children of Judas, I've always been fond of the Nelapsi, Daeva who need to devour vast quantities of blood and use their Nightmare powers to haunt their domains, collecting their tithes while the mortals are too busy worrying about a ghost that doesn't exist.<br /> <br /> This was a cool concept, but the original bloodline write-up doesn't do a lot to explore it. Much of the emphasis is placed on the bloodline's weakness, which is certainly important, but the haunting thing was a much more interesting hook. So, we refined that a bit. Our Nelapsi don't just spook their domains: they craft legends for themselves to serve as a mask over their feedings, both from mortals and from other Kindred. No one really believes the old mansion just out of town is still inhabited, but the locals just can't help go check it out every now and then. Everyone's entitled to one good scare. And no one <i>really </i>thinks the devil will show up at the crossroads if you speak his name, but...you still go and try it out, don't you? No harm in that.<br /> <br /> To this end, the bloodline's &quot;gift&quot; is actually a collection of Merits and a Devotion. Rather than an inherent trait or a special Discipline, the Nelapsi cultivate their legends through mentorships with their elders. It keeps the bloodline's population down, assuring only the worthy gain the bloodline's blessing. This tied in to some of the first edition material, but makes it a bit more immediate to players.<br /> <br /> The other big mechanical changes we made were their bane and Disciplines. We tend not to change around Discipline spreads for bloodlines that didn't have a unique one in 1E (with a couple of exceptions), but the author made a pretty compelling argument that Resilience fit a lot better than Celerity. The &quot;two hearts&quot; myth from the original bloodline was something we wanted to do more with, especially considering its built right into their logo, so we felt that was a good representation of this legend. Plus it gave us an opportunity to come up with a nifty little Merit to convert their old Devotion. I did consider giving the Obfuscate when I was doing development, but I didn't want them <i>too </i>Nosferatu. They're Daeva: creating a cool legend is the point, not the gaslighting.<br /> <br /> As for the bane, we loved the <i>idea </i>of them needing vast herds to feed an endless bloodlust, but we also really didn't like the original's implementation. Depriving players of resources always feels like a sub-optimal design choice, so, instead, the Nelapsi now <i>crave </i>more blood. The Beast gets a little taste, and then it comes roaring back if it doesn't get enough.<br /> <br /> Without further ado, enjoy the Nelapsi! Tomorrow, we'll check in with the Duchagne.<br /> <br /> (PS: I've noticed a few typos come up here and there as I excerpt these; if you've noticed them too, don't worry, I'll be doing an update of the PDF in the near future.)<br /> <br /> <b>Nelapsi: The ones who feast on you</b><br /> <br /> &quot;Don't test me. I haven't eaten.&quot;<br /> <br /> <i>You\u2019ve heard about him since the night he moved into that ominous townhouse at the end of the street. People say strange sounds and lights come through the windows in the middle of the night. The old folks cross themselves as they pass like it's haunted, and the jackoff teenage boys try to spook their girlfriends with tales of children going missing.<br /> <br /> He takes your hand, bending down to give it a little kiss. It\u2019s a bit dorky, but the charm radiates like a sunny day, and those ivory teeth shine with every inviting smile. They\u2019re having a party later tonight, he says. Come see what really goes down.<br /> <br /> How scary could it be?</i><br /> <br /> The Daeva know humans better than any Kindred, and the Nelapsi know the most primal human want of all: hunger. A Glutton can wake starving even if she entered daysleep with a bellyful of blood. Feeding grounds and herds are a painful point of necessity for these Serpents, and the source of many a neonate\u2019s downfall when she devours them all in one gory gulp. Even when Vitae is free and plentiful, feeding is a careful balance between the safety of moderation and the false promises of satisfaction.<br /> <br /> The Nelapsi didn\u2019t always believe such control was necessary. Once, they fed in whatever quantity they required, lording over private domains with only their childer for company. The Gluttons of old ruled not as royalty, but ideas, medieval legends that infested every mortal unfortunate enough to hear their tales. These were not the Daeva of dreams and fantasy, but greedy ghosts lairing in haunted castle keeps demanding tribute, or cunning demons awaiting supplicants in the low places of the earth. Each folkloric mask was a way to hide in plain sight at the top of the food chain. Even their name is just another guise, taken from a Slovakian beast that devoured livestock and killed with a glare \u2014 though, given their appetites, perhaps they gifted their name upon the monster.<br /> <br /> Cults to these nightmares once riddled Eastern Europe, from Bohemia to the Black Sea, and the bloodline held dozens of hamlets as their personal buffets. Few approached; none dared leave. And every now and then, an offering would gain favor as a Glutton\u2019s clan curse gripped its soul, and its new childe would become yet another part of its mythos.<br /> <br /> Eventually, other Kindred took up arms against these Locusts, fearful for their own herds. It was a costly war. The bloodline\u2019s terrible fortitude wasn\u2019t easily broken, and the conflict provided even more grist to weave into their tales. Some Kindred say each Nelapsi bears two souls, their appetites only sated by feeding both. Others believe they devour mortals whole and wield the strength of two men, with two hearts pumping in their chests. Still others whisper that their curse is so all-consuming that it requires a pair of mortals to die for one Embrace.<br /> <br /> Yet these stories weren\u2019t enough to save them. In the end, the Nelapsi were scattered, manses burned to ash as their human playthings were dragged away and made to forget. With the fall of the old guard came the diaspora, and a new ethos took hold to prevent future purges. The new blood\u2019s philosophy is restrained compared to that of their forebears, though its adherents prefer to call it <i>elegant</i>.<br /> <br /> Modern Nelapsi distance themselves from their herds but still forge legends. They\u2019re the friend-of-a-friend-of-an-acquaintance who can talk their way out of any situation, and they\u2019ll do the same for you if you\u2019ll meet them under the new moon. He\u2019s the party animal who knows every regular but never shares his real name; if you learn it, you can summon him for one hell of a night. She\u2019s Mephisto at the crossroads, offering wishes in exchange for a liter of your finest vintage.<br /> <br /> Rather than estates and stables of mortal morsels, tonight a Nelapsi lets his myth do the heavy lifting. His herds are vast because the story he\u2019s crafted for himself is more than the sum of its parts, and it keeps the All Night Society from ever realizing the truth of the Locust flitting through its fields. A Glutton\u2019s reputation will always precede him \u2014 for good and for ill.<br /> <br /> <b>Why you want to be us</b><br /> <br /> Even when we try to be quiet, we wind up being bigger than life. Helps that we\u2019re already dead. We can devour the world entire if it suits us; the Danse Macabre is just a frenzied summer ball before the winter chill sets in. Join us, little grasshoppers, for our larders are full and our herds are fat. We\u2019ll make sure the dancing never stops \u2014 greedily ever after.<br /> <br /> <b>Why you should fear us</b><br /> <br /> We are the virus of language, and to know our tales is to risk infection. You say our names in the mirror thrice upon a blood moon because you want the monsters to be real. You want them to spin hay to gold and chew on your firstborn\u2019s bones in recompense, ridding you of the burden. One good story is worth a thousand cattle, and we\u2019ll dine out on ours as long as you keep telling them.<br /> <br /> <b>Why we should fear ourselves</b><br /> <br /> There is a hole. Something filled it once, but nothing remains now. We can never know what we\u2019ve lost, because in each of us it\u2019s a different hollow. The Beast, in its cunning, calls us to feed and fill the void. Fill it with stories. Fill it with power. Fill it with blood. But the hole was born in life, and it can never be filled in death.<br /> <br /> <b>Parent Clan: </b>Daeva<br /> <br /> <b>Nicknames:</b> Gluttons, Locusts<br /> <br /> <b>Bloodline Bane (The Edacious Curse):</b> While every vampire needs to feed, the Locusts have a hard time stopping once they start. After a feeding scene, roll a Nelapsi\u2019s Humanity. On a failure, the vampire is [REDACTED].<br /> <br /> <b>Disciplines:</b> <i>Majesty</i>, <i>Nightmare</i>, Resilience, Vigor<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Bloodline Gift: The Lessons</b><br /> <br /> The Nelapsi pass down their ancient traditions through a rigid mentor\u2013apprentice hierarchy. Each neonate suffers through a long period of discipleship under a <i>predek </i>(\u201cancestor\u201d), usually one\u2019s own sire or a Glutton of great status. The fledgling must learn three canonical lessons from the <i>predek </i>before she can be considered her own master.<br /> <br /> Each lesson is embodied mechanically by the Merits and Devotion below.<ul><li><b>The First Lesson:</b> <i>Survival</i>, represented by the Quickened Hunger and Shadow Heart Merits. This is the most basic and practical lesson, with elders teaching their childer to use their prey efficiently in the face of their curse and to escape the wrath of fearful Kindred.</li> <li><b>The Second Lesson: </b><i>Renown</i>, represented by the Fame, Advanced Merit. This lesson isn\u2019t so much taught as discovered, as the <i>predek </i>allows his student to forge her personal legend \u2014 though how far she needs to spread this myth is up to the mentor.</li> <li><b>The Third Lesson:</b> <i>Domain</i>, represented by the Cursed Fiefdom Devotion. This lesson varies the most between adherents of the new ways and the old. Modernist Gluttons believe land is only as necessary as it is useful, and they teach their prot\u00e9g\u00e9s to incorporate territory into their mythoi on a case-by-case basis without growing attached to it. Conversely, <i>predkove </i>from the old country teach that domain is the pinnacle of a Nelapsi\u2019s legend and Requiem, and that to have land is to attain true power.</li> </ul><br /> Nelapsi characters aren\u2019t required to learn these traits in order (or at all, in theory), and some <i>predkove </i>teach the first two lessons more organically. However, they always pass on the Lesson of Domain last.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-11T15:57:04-08:00","id":1467494,"title":"","content":"Nalpsi sound pretty cool! Very interesting Bloodline they are, plus the Cursed Fiefdom Devotion sounds neat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27083-truemrmultiverse","name":"TrueMrMultiverse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27083_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-11T16:00:51-08:00","id":1467495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TrueMrMultiverse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1467058-sin-again-daeva-now-available-on-storytellers-vault-2e-requiem-clan-book?p=1467494#post1467494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nalpsi sound pretty cool! Very interesting Bloodline they are, plus the Cursed Fiefdom Devotion sounds neat.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's kind of the Majesty/Nightmare version of Oubliette or Lord of the Land. You can basically make everyone love being inside your horrible territory, and they'll think nothing of all the &quot;hauntings,&quot; but anyone who enters is immediately scared away when they see what it really is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-11T19:09:25-08:00","id":1467509,"title":"","content":"Loved the Nelapsi.<br /> <br /> But on another note, all those REDACTIONs made me think how would be an explanation on bloodlines written as an SCP article.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-11T20:02:14-08:00","id":1467514,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1467058-sin-again-daeva-now-available-on-storytellers-vault-2e-requiem-clan-book?p=1467509#post1467509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Loved the Nelapsi.<br /> <br /> But on another note, all those REDACTIONs made me think how would be an explanation on bloodlines written as an SCP article.</div> </div> </div> </div>SCP-7777: The Kindred<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-12T14:41:12-08:00","id":1467600,"title":"","content":"Alright, time to dive into the Duchagne.<br /> <br /> As noted in my Erzs\u00e9bet preview, this was my other bloodline, and similar to the Cavaliers, they went through a lot of rewrites. Partly, this stemmed from ambivalence about the original version. Daeva who can evoke extreme sensations in their victims is a strong concept, but I didn't love the execution, especially their Licencieux Discipline. I also thought that, while their French Revolution backstory was interesting, it felt a little arbitrary: the bloodline's concept feels fundamentally Daeva, but it's couched in a <i>very </i>specific time and place.<br /> <br /> The biggest difficulty was figuring out what their power should look like. I briefly considered giving them a unique Discipline, one that works similar to Celerity, Praestantia, Resilience, Vigor, or Vitiate, but I couldn't come up with a good passive power that wasn't just Vitiate with a different flavor (though, if you <i>did </i>want to translate Licencieux using that power's effects but different narrative descriptions, you could do a lot worse). Ultimately, I felt giving them all three Physical powers and then building Devotions around those worked best. The powers they ended up with are reminiscent of the Khaibit and Liderc, with a baseline that's enhanced by other effects.<br /> <br /> The other big mechanical change was their bane. I basically just threw the original out altogether, though I tried to keep with the idea that they get bored easily. Just in a very different way...<br /> <br /> As for the backstory, I ended up keeping the French connection, but suggested that Duchagne-like vampires have appeared throughout history, and the current brood is only the latest iteration. What that means for your chronicle is up to you, but we hint at a few suggestions on how to use that plot hook.<br /> <br /> Anyway, here's the Duchagne. <s>That brings us to the end of our bloodlines; I have some thoughts I'd like to share on the Erzsebet and Xiao that I'll post tomorrow, but otherwise, I think I'll talk about the Blowouts chapter next, probably on Monday.</s> I'm wrong, we've still got the Gulikan! We'll do them tomorrow.<br /> <br /> <b>Duchagne: The ones who inflame you</b><br /> <br /> &quot;I know what you need, but you haven't earned it.&quot;<br /> <br /> Physical pleasure is too often dismissed as indolence. Mammals evolved to feel good \u2014 it keeps the young occupied and the mature focused on fucking. By the same token, pain also has its uses: Don\u2019t touch the hot stove; don\u2019t step on the broken glass; don\u2019t let the dead thing bite you. Pain is a medium, and handled with care it offers its own delights. Yet the Kindred think they\u2019ve grown beyond these drives. What earthly delight response matches a Kiss on the throat or Vitae on the tongue? Human sensation is a shadow of what a vampire can do just by bleeding.<br /> <br /> To this, the Duchagne say, give us five minutes.<br /> <br /> Call a Duchagne a hedonist and she\u2019ll ask why you aren\u2019t one too. The Embrace brings a silver platter of corruptions, but the Kindred act as if they\u2019re on a diet, distracting themselves from the raw joys of death with intrigues and schemes. Not that there\u2019s anything wrong with a good scheme, but vampires who make them the focus of the Requiem are missing the point of being dead. The Decadents know tending the body is the only worthwhile occupation, and with <i>les arts licencieux</i>, they take reign over sense memory, introducing beautiful pain and terrible pleasure to the human body in pursuit of a far more refined meal than blood alone can offer.<br /> <br /> But this isn\u2019t just for sadism the sake of sadism. A Decadent can squeeze more Vitae from her victims by flooding them with the very essence of life. Of course, most Kindred hear about these practices and go straight to the trite \u2014 fuzzy handcuffs and spanky sex and bodice rippers \u2014 but the Duchagne didn\u2019t get where they are tonight by settling for clich\u00e9s.<br /> <br /> Take a trip with the tour guide. He brings his customers to all the places they won\u2019t tell you about, the secret underbellies where real history festers like a wound. You can almost feel the bullet hit your chest where the mafia don got whacked, and your breath grows short where the lovely heiress dropped herself in the river.<br /> <br /> Meet the insult comic. He defines your flaws in needle-sharp patter, and the resultant laughter tears through you like a chemical burn. Your flesh is rawer than a sunburn, but the balm is so soothing as he rips everyone else to pieces too.<br /> <br /> Chat with the phone sex gal. She doesn\u2019t look a day past 60 at 120, but that voice still flows like caramel. Tastes like it too. She made a fortune helping lonely hearts remember the good old days, but these nights she just does it for fun.<br /> <br /> The modern Decadents first emerged in the French Revolution, but they had predecessors, cults to hedonism the All Night Society still recalls with shame and envy. All bloodlines claim contradictory origins, but the Duchagne can confirm a few of them. Elders with the same blood as the French clutch say they were Yangists in the Warring States, spreading the ethics of egoism among the All Night Society, and a handful remember lustful nights as Pan worshippers, ministering erotic floggings on behalf of pre-Acolyte cults. Records and common legends of the bloodline\u2019s powers confirm these claims, and at least a dozen origin myths follow them from continent to continent. It\u2019s as if the bloodline were a natural gravity the Daeva fall toward every few centuries \u2014 one that burns bright, then out. Only a handful of these elders still exist, and all claim their branch collapsed in a spectacular manner, whether from infighting or Kindred intervention. Perhaps this is the ultimate expression of their egoism: If you\u2019ve got to go, better take everyone with you.<br /> <br /> <b>Why you want to be us</b><br /> <br /> With us, you can to turn their nerves into a Swarovski crystal of sensation, salting the meat in ways no other Lick would dare to dream. Fair warning: You probably won\u2019t make it. You\u2019re not good enough yet, and maybe you\u2019ll never be. But you don\u2019t get anywhere without trying, do you?<br /> <br /> <b>Why you should fear us</b><br /> <br /> Ever had an itch you can\u2019t scratch? Let\u2019s be more specific: Did you ever have an itch you had to wrench your shoulder to reach? One that wouldn\u2019t go away with a metric ton of ointment or powder or heroin. One you couldn\u2019t dent no matter how deep you dug through the skin. Yeah. That sure would suck.<br /> <br /> <b>Why we should fear ourselves</b><br /> <br /> There\u2019s a point where the human body hardens to pleasure. You only have so many ways to get people off, and joy is so individual. But pain? Pain is facile, and if you let it be the answer to every question, doling it out will be the only way you ever feel again.<br /> <br /> <b>Parent Clan: </b>Daeva<br /> <br /> <b>Nicknames: </b>Decadents, Bacchantes<br /> <br /> <b>Bloodline Bane (The Sybaritic Curse):</b> It\u2019s all so tiresome. The Kiss, the Blood, the Beast \u2014 all of it. To feel alive, Duchagne need something bracing to wake their dead nerves, or otherwise the Beast will find ways to gratify itself. Unless a Decadent experiences intense physical sensation as she feeds (pain, pleasure, extremes of temperature, etc.), she [REDACTED].<br /> <br /> <b>Disciplines: </b>Celerity, <i>Majesty</i>, Resilience, Vigor<br /> <br /> <b>Bloodline Origins</b><ul><li>In the time of the French Revolution, a noble of the Invictus burned for her crimes. If any Lick deserved the flame, it was the Viscountess du Chagne. Embraced in a time when feudalism was radical, she spent her Requiem spreading misery for her own indulgence, torturing or exalting victims depending on her whim. Her boudoir was a place of beautiful agonies, and even her allies in the First Estate thought she got what was coming to her. The Carthians called her not just a counter*revolutionary, but an abomination, sentencing her to Hell by setting the flames on the Devil\u2019s behalf. Yet even the inferno couldn\u2019t match her lust. Some say she rose from the pyre and demanded the coals be made hotter, while others swear claim an unwitting double took her place. Whatever the truth, her brush with oblivion crystalized her philosophy, and she began a spree of Embraces across France. Most Decadents tonight trace their blood and name to the Viscountess, venerating her in the hope she\u2019ll never turn her debauched eye on them.</li> <li>Before Viscountess du Chagne ever pissed off the Revolution, other Decadents ravaged their way through history. Their earliest antecedents were Cyrenaics and Epicureans in Ancient Greece, forming mystery cults to Dionysus, Pan, Zeus, and other oversexed gods. They were called Maenads in those nights, and their few survivors claim they fell in one bloody frenzy. So the story goes, they were the ones who devoured Orpheus, and drunk on the blood of the perfect muse, they ripped themselves asunder for the sheer pleasure of the act. A few of these Kindred still exist, along with Serpents from other parts of the world with similar tales of decadence and destruction. Wherever the Bacchantes rise, a fall is sure to follow.</li> <li>The Duchagne aren\u2019t a bloodline at all, just a perversion that draws Clan Daeva ever closer to oblivion. Are they a disease? A curse? Evolution? Whatever else they are, they\u2019re right about being the ultimate expression of their clan, but only in the sense that they\u2019re a logical extreme. Every time they reappear, they return more virulent, and this French brood is especially resistant to destruction. For now. Some night, they might just gobble up the entire Serpent clan, and if they do, their inevitable destruction will spread through the All Night Society like a forest fire, entire domains succumbing to paroxysms of orgy and death. All Kindred will feel their destruction, and they won\u2019t be able to get enough of it.</li> </ul><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":192,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","user":"Yossarian","date":". 11-13-2021, 02:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-12T17:18:35-08:00","id":1467616,"title":"","content":"The Duchagne are very interesting! Like the implication they\u2019re a weird cyclical bloodline that rises and falls in different forms throughout history.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27083-truemrmultiverse","name":"TrueMrMultiverse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27083_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-13T12:26:04-08:00","id":1467704,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TrueMrMultiverse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1467058-sin-again-daeva-now-available-on-storytellers-vault-2e-requiem-clan-book?p=1467616#post1467616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Duchagne are very interesting! Like the implication they\u2019re a weird cyclical bloodline that rises and falls in different forms throughout history.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was a plot thread that (hopefully) expands the bloodline's potential for stories, especially historical ones, but also still honours the original. I didn't use all of the French aristocracy backstory, but there's enough of it there that you can fit it in with the old material. And really, if someone likes the old lore better, it's super easy to use that and just incorporate the new mechanics.<br /> <br /> Anyway, today let's take a whiff of the Gulikan!<br /> <br /> This is probably the bloodline that changed the least in the book; mostly, we've just streamlined it and made it a little more accessible. They're still perfumer Daeva who owe allegiance to a vast hierarchy back in Istanbul. The author added a few plot threads and strange details to their possible origins, but generally this is pretty true to the first version. Even their bane isn't too different from their (novel-length) original weakness.<br /> <br /> The biggest change came with Ortam, in that it didn't really live up to its concept. The basic power was decent, but its ability to produce Discipline effects through scent was nigh useless. So, we kept that fundamental power and went about creating some proper recipes for it. These are more like &quot;distillations&quot; of Disciplines, and unlike the original power, you can produce them with donations from other Kindred, rather than needing to know every single one yourself, which we felt was a bit too much of a roadblock. We also realized, for a bloodline of characters who sniff things all the time, they weren't particularly good at discerning scents. So, we gave them some inherent abilities to go with Ortam; it's a Discipline that requires a lot of buy-in, so I felt players should get some bennies for making that investment. Originally, that was going to be an inherent quality, but my feeling is, if you've got a unique bloodline Discipline, you don't need an inherent gift as well.<br /> <br /> In development, <i>very </i>little changed for this bloodline. The bane went through some tweaking, but other than that, it was a very clean draft.<br /> <br /> But enough out of me; reacquaint yourselves with the Gulikan. Tomorrow I think I'll take a day off, but Monday I'll be back with my dev commentary for the Xiao and Erzs\u00e9bet, and then we'll get into Blowouts.<br /> <br /> <b>Gulikan: The ones who breathe you in</b><br /> <br /> &quot;What shall I make out of you?&quot;<br /> <br /> To smell something is to literally take a tiny bit of it into yourself, adding a sliver of its substance to your own. In humans, this connection is fleeting. With our stunted noses and laughable sense of smell, all but the most obvious scents pass us by, barely perceived. But Kindred aren\u2019t human. They can sense the scab where you cut yourself shaving from all the way down the block, and they can follow its sweet aroma right to your door. If blood is life, then by taking in its scent, are you not capturing a person\u2019s very essence for yourself? The Gulikan certainly think so.<br /> <br /> All vampires excite at the coppery delight of blood, but the Perfumers relish it almost as much as the act of feeding. For them, scent isn\u2019t just truth \u2014 it\u2019s the only truth. Originating out of the former Ottoman Empire, but now found all over the world, the Gulikan aren\u2019t just better at smelling blood than other Kindred; they can extract something essential from it, a special quality only they can perceive. This ability to draw out blood\u2019s true essence allows them to manipulate Vitae and infuse supernatural qualities into perfumes, soaps, incense, candles, and more. A Perfumer\u2019s works are of exquisite beauty and quality, and turn an even more attractive profit.<br /> <br /> Would you like to waltz into the VIP section of the club and instantly own it? Just a spritz of Serpent\u2019s Enticement, and all the pretty people will be hanging off your every word. Tired of not getting the respect you deserve? Authority for Lords will have mortals scrambling for the privilege of obeying your every random whim. Sick of being pushed around? A dose of Haunt\u2019s Spite will turn you from milquetoast to terror in an instant. More than anything, the Gulikan bottle power and sell it at a premium.<br /> <br /> With such effectiveness and versatility behind them, the Gulikan\u2019s wares are always in demand. Of course, if other Kindred realized the truth of these heavenly scents, there might be a boycott. Vitae is the active ingredient for everything created by Ortam, and that Vitae is most often donated by the Perfumer herself. Every time you take a deep breath of the exquisite jasmine-and-honeysuckle blend prepared by your local Gulikan, you\u2019re also breathing in her blood. The Perfumers certainly don\u2019t advertise this little side-effect of their wares; they prefer to keep their influence on their clients \u201csubtle.\u201d If a person is more favorable to a Gulikan after sampling her stock, more willing to listen to her suggestions in public, well, chalk it up to customer satisfaction.<br /> <br /> The Perfumers are an organized and haughty family, with high standards for who joins. The Old Masters who guide the bloodline from their seat in Istanbul supposedly have records of every Gulikan ever Embraced, as well as lists of their accomplishments. This regimented structure ensures Perfumers aren\u2019t competing with each other in the same domains (with the notable exception of Istanbul itself), and guarantees the worthiest \u2014 read: most obedient \u2014 students receive training in Ortam. This decadent tower has stood for centuries, though in recent nights, it\u2019s started to show some cracks along its base.<br /> <br /> Objects created by Perfumers are notoriously beautiful, not only for the exquisite odors they produce, but for the artistry of their presentation. The thing is, they don\u2019t have to be. A candle infused with a Haunt\u2019s blood will ward an area with fear whether it\u2019s delicately carved to resemble a pillar of weeping skulls or just a rough wax cylinder with a wick stuck in the top. In short, as long as it\u2019s functional, the form makes no difference. Realizing this, many neonate Gulikan chafe under the Old Masters\u2019 rules and restrictions, especially those Perfumers half-way across the globe from Turkey. Why should they have to pick up and move to a different domain when they can compete by selling their wares at half the cost? Why should their goods be exclusive to the already wealthy and powerful?<br /> <br /> Like most elders, the Old Masters don\u2019t appreciate being questioned, and their counter-arguments in favor of the traditional hierarchy have been rather pointed \u2014 lethally so, in most cases. Still, their reach can only extend so far, and while they may dismiss these radical youths as nothing more than common Peddlers, the movement is growing. Why buy from the master when you can get the apprentice to make the same thing for a song? Sure, it won\u2019t make you weep blood tears with its ethereal beauty, but you\u2019ll still be able to make rent at the end of the month.<br /> <br /> <b>Why you want to be us</b><br /> <br /> We have it all: wealth, respect, and product that moves. We can bottle fear, spray-on authority, and people will pay us ridiculous amounts of money for just a sniff. And don\u2019t you want to smell amazing for all eternity?<br /> <br /> <b>Why you should fear us</b><br /> <br /> Weren\u2019t you listening? We have it all. All the money, all the prestige, all the power. We have every weapon of the Blood at our disposal, and with one errant breath, we\u2019ll have you too.<br /> <br /> <b>Why we should fear ourselves</b><br /> <br /> We have it all, but it\u2019s never enough. We obsess over the next scent, trying to perfect it, to realize it to its fullest perfection, and take it in until there\u2019s nothing left\u2026 then we move on to the next one and do it all over again. Eventually, \u201cthe next one\u201d is going to be \u201cthe last one.\u201d<br /> <br /> <b>Parent Clan: </b>Daeva<br /> <br /> <b>Nicknames:</b> Perfumers, Bloodhounds, Peddlers<br /> <br /> <b>Bloodline Bane (The Hyperosmic Curse): </b>Whenever a Perfumer has more than passing intimate contact with a living person, which can range from an involved conversation, to a nasty ground fight, or even to sex, they must roll Humanity. On a failure, [REDACTED].<br /> <br /> <b>Disciplines: </b>Celerity, <i>Majesty</i>, <i>Ortam</i>, Vigor<br /> <br /> <b>Ortam (Excerpt)</b><br /> <br /> The end result of the Gulikan\u2019s art and obsession, Ortam is their most carefully-guarded secret. Using an arcane combination of alchemy, chemistry, and blood sorcery, Perfumers can render Vitae down to its purest essence, extracting enchanting and terrifying scents. They then trap these scents within perfumes, incense, candles, pomades, and more. The resulting items are infused with effects that echo different Disciplines, based on the recipe the Gulikan used.<br /> <br /> Ortam works in two parts. First is the basic practice of extracting the essential scent of Vitae, the crafting of an item to house it, and the binding the former to the latter. The second is the recipe, the specific effect the Gulikan is trying to create. Not so much a single progressive Discipline as it is a different way to employ the Beast\u2019s arsenal, Ortam is incredibly versatile. One of its chief strengths, however, is subtlety. Kindred are used to guarding their eyes and ears against the dangers of an imprinted command or dulcet word, but few are vigilant against an enticing scent carried on the breeze.<br /> <br /> <b>Ortam Recipes</b><br /> <br /> The eleven recipes outlined below are the most common, but variants exist, and rumors persist of more exotic formulas that can mimic unique abilities possessed by bloodlines and lost clans. There are even whispers of secret recipes that use the blood of werewolves, fae beings, and even stranger things\u2026<br /> <br /> <b>Essence Vitale Absolue</b><br /> <br /> <b>Duration: </b>Scene<br /> <br /> <b>Effect: </b>The essential Ortam ability can be crafted with Vitae from any vampire, creating an intoxicating scent that ensnares minds as it delights them. Smelling Essence Vitale Absolue is the same as having tasted the donor vampire\u2019s blood. It can establish a Vinculum, though it can\u2019t increase an extant one, and it provides no sustenance. Any mortals taking in the scent are helpless against it, but Kindred reflexively resist with Resolve + Blood Potency \u2013 Ortam, shaking off the would-be bond with a successful roll.<br /> <br /> Essence Vitale Absolue is the only Ortam recipe that can be combined with others; this requires the vampire to spend an additional Vitae per dose, but he still only needs to make one roll.<br /> <br /> <b>Animalism: Tiger Musk</b><br /> <br /> <b>Duration: </b>Scene<br /> <br /> <b>Effect:</b> A thick, intimidating odor that tells man and beast alike a predator is in their midst. Anyone wearing this scent enjoys the rote quality on all rolls involving the Animal Ken and Intimidation Skills, as long as the target of these actions can smell them.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":192,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","user":"Yossarian","date":". 11-13-2021, 05:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-15T13:18:03-08:00","id":1467913,"title":"","content":"Happy Monday, all!<br /> <br /> Today, we'll talk about the Erzs\u00e9bet and the Xiao. I was going to include something on Blowouts (what we're calling our social gathering system), but I think that deserves its own post, so we'll cover that tomorrow.<br /> <br /> Here are the original previews:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1466506-erzsebet-2e-sin-again-daeva-preview\">Erzsebet</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1466167-california-xiao-2e-sin-again-daeva-preview\">Xiao</a><br /> <br /> Let's start with the <b>Erzs\u00e9bet</b>, so that I can get typing the accented E out of the way for the foreseeable future.<br /> <br /> The Cavaliers went through a lot of revision. The 1E version is really great (iconic, even), but I wanted to offer a few more reasons to join them. They also have a pretty nasty bane, but I wanted that to feel more immediate, as aging can be easy to gloss over in a short chronicle. I also wanted to do away with making them infirm, which isn't a bad idea at all (slowly rotting until you wither to nothing), but I felt like the Masquerade danger of their curse was the more interesting thread to follow in Second Edition.<br /> <br /> That said, it took a long time to get where it where it needed to be. My first idea was that Erzs\u00e9bet have difficulty relating to other immortals, and that this sets them apart as insular members of the All Night Society. However, the more I developed the piece, the more that felt like the wrong choice. The original Erzs\u00e9bet are a bit shady in the eyes of other vampires, but they're not aloof. It also felt like too much of a social disadvantage for a bunch of scheming Daeva who seem to have conned much of their fortune out of their Kindred. But, I still wanted something that would matter more night-to-night. So, I took the idea of their aging and put it into overdrive: The Erzs\u00e9bet can now age rapidly whenever they suffer a breaking point. This is just a year, and you get to roll Humanity to prevent it, but those years can really start to rack up if you've been acting like a monster. They still age slowly, but now that's a given, not something tied to torpor. They can <i>revert </i>their aging now with sleep, but once a Cavalier hits Humanity 6, she'll always be on the clock.<br /> <br /> Because this bane was going to be more immediate, I also wanted their benefits to be a bit meatier. Initially, I kind of hedged my bets, and gave them a few extras for the blush of life...but then I thought, screw it, they always have the blush. The Erzs\u00e9bet are always just a little more alive than other Kindred, and while that comes with a serious downside, it also allows them to relate to kine in a way other Serpents simply can't. I also gave them a couple of Merits and Devotions to represent their immense wealth and their &quot;enhanced&quot; relationship with humans.<br /> <br /> Another cut element was Solace. Solace appears elsewhere in the book, but originally I'd tied it to the Withered. I'll talk a little bit about how this was supposed to work when I do an entry on Solace specifically, but basically, it just didn't fit in the context of a bloodline.<br /> <br /> Narratively, the Cavaliers aren't too different from their original version. I tweaked their presentation a bit, presenting the idea that their main avenue of entertainment is fraud on their Kindred and the kine (in very different ways), but generally, if you liked their 1E version, I think you'll recognize them in this 2E one. And of course, there is the prerequisite David Bowie reference; some things never change.<br /> <br /> Now, let's talk about the <b>Xiao</b>.<br /> <br /> The Xiao are another bloodline that's not that different from the original. They still run a cult that steals emotions, and they still have a schism of apostates who hate them. Because we made Kingjan into a Style Merit for the Sect instead of a Discipline, we also wanted to give the Apostates some mechanical weight. So, we offer a few &quot;anti-emotional&quot; Devotions for them to pick up in the fight against their cousins and their cult.<br /> <br /> This bloodline didn't change a lot in development, though I did ask that the Apostates be made, for lack of a better term, meaner. While they may abhor the Sect, they're just as much leeches on society, just in different ways. Instead of just being slightly benighted conscientious objectors, they're ruthless loners who do dirty work for the All Night Society, leveraging their muted emotions as a way to handle the tasks no one else wants.<br /> <br /> The other thing we wanted to cover briefly was this bloodline's relationship with the Tianp\u00e0n Xiao. Although we don't come out and say &quot;they're related,&quot; we did want more of a plot hook for their relationship than <b>Bloodlines: The Chosen </b>offers. They certainly could just have the same name by coincidence (they might not even exist in the same chronicle, if you don't want them to), but we felt that a little bit of ambiguity was more interesting, especially considering each bloodlines' differing relationship with the Ordo Dracul.<br /> <br /> Mechanically, apart from replacing Kingjan with Nightmare, the other major mechanical change was their bane. The original isn't bad mechanically, but we wanted to move away from references to real-life mental disorders. Instead of being &quot;sociopaths&quot; the Xiao now have increased difficulty in relating to humans. Their bane is a bit of a riff on the Nosferatu curse, but both a bit narrower and a bit nastier.<br /> <br /> Anyway, that's it for today. Tomorrow, we move on to Blowouts \u2014 for real this time!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":192,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","user":"Yossarian","date":". 11-15-2021, 06:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-15T13:31:45-08:00","id":1467917,"title":"","content":"The first link to the Erzs\u00e9bet in the above post seems to be faulty; might be a mobile thing, but still.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-15T15:08:42-08:00","id":1467929,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1467058-sin-again-daeva-now-available-on-storytellers-vault-2e-requiem-clan-book?p=1467917#post1467917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The first link to the Erzs\u00e9bet in the above post seems to be faulty; might be a mobile thing, but still.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fixed! I think it didn't like the accented e in the link? That's the only thing I changed.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-15T17:43:36-08:00","id":1467949,"title":"","content":"Since I'm Brazilian my keyboard is well equipped to type accented \u00e9 or to put \u00b4 over any letter, but it took me some time to learn how to put \u00af for writing things like T\u014dky\u014d properly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-15T17:55:28-08:00","id":1467951,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1467058-sin-again-daeva-now-available-on-storytellers-vault-2e-requiem-clan-book?p=1467949#post1467949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since I'm Brazilian my keyboard is well equipped to type accented \u00e9 or to put \u00b4 over any letter, but it took me some time to learn how to put \u00af for writing things like T\u014dky\u014d properly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Writing White Wolf-adjacent stuff makes one <i>intimately </i>familiar with the keyboard code for em-dashes (\u2014). We love our em-dashes in the World of Darkness.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-16T13:54:01-08:00","id":1468046,"title":"","content":"Hello all! Let's move on from bloodlines and get to the special &quot;thing&quot; chapter of the book: Blowouts.<br /> <br /> In each of these books, the second chapter has been dedicated to a special subsystem that's associated with the supplement's particular clan. In <b>Strange Shades</b>, this was Shadow Cults, in <b>Better Feared </b>this was Necropoli, and in <b>False Gods </b>this was Malkavia. All three of these systems are based on material in the First Edition clan books. But when we get to <b>Kiss of the Succubus</b>, there isn't really anything like that. The Cacophony is <i>kind </i><i>of </i>that, but it's covered by a Merit, and one that was updated in the Second Edition rulebook anyway. There wasn't really much to add to the Cacophony (apart from a couple of Merits here and there), so that left us with a lot of room to come up with something new.<br /> <br /> Parties in <b>Vampire </b>chronicles are almost a given. Elysium is often framed as having a festive atmosphere, and <b>Fall of the Camarilla </b>famously begins with the coterie being assigned to throw a party. Parties, of course, aren't just a Daeva thing, but this is true of the other special systems in the series as well. Malkavia isn't tied to the Ventrue so much as its tied to their Discipline, and Shadow Cults are by far more common for Mekhet to start, but any clan could put one together in a pinch (and trust me, they do). The Warrens system is probably the only one that's <i>really </i>unique to the clan, but even then, we were able to include a few story seeds about other vampires having similar, exclusive domains.<br /> <br /> Still, parties are probably the loosest connection to the associated clan, overall, so we made a point to focus on Daeva viewpoints (both from within and without), as well as their clan Discipline, Majesty. We also wanted to go into some history: what kind of ragers were the Daeva throwing in the Middle Ages? That became a little bit of a micro <b>Dark Eras</b>.<br /> <br /> I also wanted to cover Genres. Parties come in many forms, but it's all too easy to fall into cliches with vampires: underground nightclubs or to-dos at the opera. Not that there's anything wrong with those, but I thought an exploration of different &quot;kinds&quot; of parties would be useful to players and Storytellers. The Genres are easily my favourite part of the chapter; the author took my very basic initial ideas and expanded them into something way cooler. There are a lot of really fun and weird story hooks in that section, so if you're running a party in your next chronicle, have a look.<br /> <br /> That brings us to systems. <b>Vampire </b>has had a few social subsystems over the years, allll the way back to <b>Succubus Club: Dead Man's Party </b>for <b>Vampire: The Masquerade</b>. However, the one thing I <i>didn't </i>want to do was Social combat. A, because <b>Guide to the Night </b>already did that, and B because I don't really <i>like </i>social combat systems. I know Social maneuvering doesn't get a lot of love, but I think it works quite well without bogging down players with a lot of additional traits to keep track of.<br /> <br /> But, if we weren't going to do Social combat, we still needed something to create conflict. And where does a lot of conflict come from? Comedy.<br /> <br /> While you can play the Blowout system straight (the example in the book isn't particularly comedic, for instance), it was very much born out of my love of sitcoms. Parties in sitcoms always go horribly wrong. Add vampires to that mix, and they go <i>catastrophically </i>wrong. They have weird interlopers who can turn invisible, they have blood dolls dying left and right because the prince didn't get her O negative, they have thousand-year rivalries coming to a head \u2014 Kindred parties are disasters waiting to happen, and disasters are always more fun than when things go smoothly, at least in a role-playing game. And the rewards of throwing an awesome party for a bunch of vampires (even one that derails a bit) can be quite lucrative.<br /> <br /> Fun fact: this is one of the few times I've done playtesting for these books. I always try to get second opinions on powers and things, but this system needed a test run that I couldn't accomplish in my own head. I think I said this above, but it was some of the most fun I've had running an RPG in quite some time.<br /> <br /> So, here's a little excerpt from the Blowout system, as well as some of the sample &quot;Social Tilts&quot;. Tomorrow, I think we'll start getting into the antagonists chapter, though I might sample a few Devotions from the systems chapter as well...<br /> <br /> <b>Up All Night: Blowout Systems</b><br /> <br /> Throwing a vampire party is easier said than done. There\u2019s a reason Elysium Masters are well-paid positions in most domains, and every covenant has its own specialized roles for handling social gatherings. Even the Dragons have a guy who maintains emergency procedures in case a good time breaks out.<br /> <br /> Kindred don\u2019t throw parties just to entertain each other, though. Vampires are users. They only put themselves out if they want something, and they never send out invitations unless they want something big.<br /> <br /> The following is a player-facing system for hosting parties and other social gatherings in the Danse Macabre, a special form of Social maneuvering Kindred characters can employ to climb the cannibal totem pole with a little help from their friends.<br /> <br /> <b>Stage One: Planning</b><br /> <br /> Being eternal, Kindred can spend decades plotting out every minute of a social gathering, but even a spontaneous party needs a little prep.<br /> <br /> <b>Goals</b><br /> <br /> First, decide on the party\u2019s goal: What are the characters trying to accomplish? Do they have a specific agenda in mind, or are they just trying to make a name for themselves in the All Night Society? Has an elder or another important figure tasked them with a particular agenda, or is the party a front for a more devious scheme?<br /> <br /> Second, each player should decide what their character\u2019s individual goal is. Are they sucking up to a superior? Trying to humiliate a rival? Or are they just putting on a show to be seen?<br /> Finally, decide what kind of party it is, and how big it should be (see \u201cGenres\u201d on p. 75 if you need inspiration). Who\u2019s on the guest list: one covenant only or every bloodsucker in town? What do the attendees hope to gain by attending: prestige, protection, or opportunity? And what kind of entertainments might they expect: a feast, a game, or a seduction? What about all three?<br /> <br /> <b>Cheap, Fast, Good</b><br /> <br /> Once the players decide on the party\u2019s goal, they need to figure out how to accomplish it. Are they putting a lot of money into it? How about effort? And what kind of timeline do they have?<br /> This step follows the old Cheap, Fast, Good principle, more formally known as the project management triangle. You can have two, but that means the one you leave out is going to make your night more difficult. A party will always have an element you have to work around, and that defines how the characters will go about their planning and hosting. Choose one of the following categories to discard; this choice applies a mechanical and narrative disadvantage to the party (see p. 84).<br /> <br /> <b>Cheap</b><br /> <br /> The coterie can get this done without a lot of resources, though you\u2019ll have to sacrifice speed or quality. A Cheap party doesn\u2019t mean it\u2019s poor quality (that\u2019s what Good is for). You can still put on a rave with Solo cups and a boombox.<br /> <br /> <b>System: </b>Blowouts that lack the Cheap quality gain the Expensive Social Tilt.<br /> <br /> <b>Fast</b><br /> <br /> Your coterie is equipped to handle whatever time constraint their planning falls under, even if they have to spend a lot of money or patch over the rough edges.<br /> <br /> The word Fast here is a bit relative. Five hours is more than enough leadup time to cover a small gathering, whereas six months is barely enough to cover a large convention. It\u2019s more that parties that lack this quality don\u2019t have <i>enough </i>time.<br /> <br /> <b>System: </b>Blowouts that lack the Fast quality gain the Delicate Timing Social Tilt.<br /> <br /> <b>Good</b><br /> <br /> You want the best of the best. That might mean spending a lot of money or taking a lot of time, but it\u2019ll be worth it in the end.<br /> <br /> Parties that lack this quality aren\u2019t necessarily \u201cbad.\u201d Neglecting Good just means the coterie had to break out a lot of duct tape and prayer. They can still achieve their goal, but maybe only by the skin of their fangs.<br /> <br /> <b>System: </b>Blowouts that lack the Good quality gain the High Stress Social Tilt.<br /> <br /> <b>Difficulty</b><br /> <br /> Murphy\u2019s Law is the only law at a Blowout, and when you throw Kindred in the mix, its many codicils are on full display. Social Tilts represent obstacles the coterie must resolve over the course of the night, with the exception of the one from Cheap/Fast/Good.<br /> <br /> <b>System: </b>The Storyteller chooses a number of Tilts to apply based on the coterie\u2019s goal and how difficult it will be to accomplish. Bigger goals mean bigger Blowouts, and bigger Blowouts mean bigger problems. However, they also mean the players have more chances to rack up Beats. A party should never have fewer than three Tilts at minimum or more than ten at maximum; consult the chart below for guidelines (see p. 85 for sample Social Tilts).<br /> <br /> Each Tilt takes a scene to resolve. To start, the coterie has a number of scenes to complete their Blowout equal to total Tilts, but this will change throughout the night.<br /> At this stage, the Storyteller only needs to state the number of Tilts she\u2019ll be applying to the Blowout. When the Hosting stage begins, she reveals them as they come up, though she can reveal them all at once if she wants to give the players a preview of what they\u2019re in for.<br /> <br /> <b>Prep</b><br /> <br /> Once the troupe decides on all of these terms and limitations, each player narrates their character\u2019s main contribution to the Blowout. They don\u2019t need to go into detail; they just need to explain how they accomplished the task. These preparations must be within a character\u2019s financial means, social status, and individual capability, mundane or otherwise.<br /> <br /> As long as this action is in a character\u2019s wheelhouse, no roll is required, but if the character wants to swing for the fences, break out the dice. Failure doesn\u2019t mean she didn\u2019t contribute, it just means she only scraped things together at the last minute. She cannot dramatically fail or exceptionally succeed; this is simply a pass or fail roll. This action comes into play in the Hosting stage, below.<br /> <br /> A character can also choose to shirk her responsibilities to focus on herself. If a player forgoes a prep action for his character, she refreshes a Willpower. She performs the bare minimum but doesn\u2019t go out of her way for the rest of the coterie.<br /> <br /> <b>Stage Two: Hosting</b><br /> <br /> [REDACTED]<br /> <br /> <b>Stage Three: Aftermath</b><br /> <br /> [REDACTED]<br /> <br /> <b>Social Tilts</b><br /> <br /> The following are examples of the kinds of problems that might arise during the coterie\u2019s party. Descriptions are fairly general, with plenty of room to tailor them to the specifics of your chronicle, and Storytellers should feel free to come up with their own if none of these suit the story. You can also treat Tilts as multipart, representing several events with only one narrative thread. This can avoid making the party too fragmented, although some troupes might enjoy the chaos.<br /> <br /> Social Tilts are written with a lighter tone, but that doesn\u2019t mean your Blowout has to be a comedy of errors. All of these scenarios can be played straight, and are good prompts for serious drama. However, you can absolutely lean into the sitcom tropes if you want to. The Kindred don\u2019t like to admit it, but <i>What We Do in the Shadows </i>is much closer to the All Night Society than they would have you believe. Daeva are especially prone to this kind of farce; sometimes being the most human also means being the biggest idiot.<br /> <br /> <b>Cancellation</b><br /> <br /> <b>Description: </b>The band is stuck on the interstate with two flats in bumper-to-bumper traffic in the middle of an ice storm on the Thanksgiving weekend.<br /> <br /> <b>Possible Resolutions: </b>Recruit a guest to perform; become the entertainment; strike up some interesting conversations.<br /> <br /> <b>Somebody Died!</b><br /> <br /> <b>Description: </b>Well, <i>shit</i>. Some greedy Lick fed too much, and now you\u2019ve got a dead blood doll or ghoul on your hands. Or maybe some mortal\u2019s heart just gave out taking coke on the toilet. In any case, you\u2019d better smooth things over.<br /> <br /> <b>Possible Resolutions:</b> Make it look like they died somewhere else; <i>Weekend at Renfield\u2019s</i>; the Embrace\u2026?<br /> <br /> <b>Vermin</b><br /> <br /> <b>Description: </b>Some Savage brought his entourage, or the photos of this place were deceptive, or the coterie just overestimated its \u201crustic\u201d charms. However it happened, the venue is crawling with rats, or roaches, or both (or worse), and it\u2019s only going to get worse before it gets better. In any event, tread lightly.<br /> <br /> <b>Possible Resolutions:</b> Call a very subtle exterminator before anyone notices; lean into it; negotiate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=