ode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1467058-sin-again-daeva-now-available-on-storytellers-vault-2e-requiem-clan-book?p=1468079#post1468079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Low Humanity's a hell of a drug.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lovely, dark, and bitter-pretending-towards-sweet.<br /> <br /> Parties indulging prey are all the more entertaining when the definition of prey is fluid.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also, since I haven't mentioned it yet, Gah, I love this soruce book. I need to find some of my favorite quotes in it, and the little flourishes like the perpetuations of B-names in the Blowout chapter make it all bounce.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 11-16-2021, 08:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-16T18:21:14-08:00","id":1468084,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1467058-sin-again-daeva-now-available-on-storytellers-vault-2e-requiem-clan-book?p=1468082#post1468082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lovely, dark, and bitter-pretending-towards-sweet.<br /> <br /> Parties indulging prey are all the more entertaining when the definition of prey is fluid.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also, since I haven't mentioned it yet, Gah, I love this soruce book. I need to find some of my favorite quotes in it, and the little flourishes like the perpetuations of B-names in the Blowout chapter make it all bounce.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you! &lt;3 Please feel free to quote; I sometimes worry I'm just bloviating to myself in these threads.<br /> <br /> As for the B-names (since this was Blowouts day): In my outline, I had three genre suggestions: Balls, Bacchanals, and Block Parties. I didn't <i>intend </i>to have them all start with B, but I'd already called the chapter Blowouts, so I vaguely suggested to the author I assigned to roll with that theme, not expecting she'd actually come up with four more of them. Even both the sidebars start with B in that section. My only real regret is that I couldn't think of a good synonym for &quot;Genres&quot; that started with B (or at least one that wasn't a huge stretch).<br /> <br /> But yeah, the B name thing was part of an effort to take the book in a different tonal direction than the other three supplements. It's all a little sexier and funnier; not lighthearted, but like the Daeva themselves, a bit more devil-may-care.I'm particularly fond of the in-character discussion of what kind of parties the <i>other </i>clans put on, which the author really nailed in terms of snotty passive aggression.<br /> <br /> <b>Kiss of the Succubus</b> also had a more ironic tone than the other clan books, and I didn't want to lose that quality. I think we made out pretty well on that front.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-16T19:12:14-08:00","id":1468088,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1467058-sin-again-daeva-now-available-on-storytellers-vault-2e-requiem-clan-book?p=1468084#post1468084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thank you! &lt;3 Please feel free to quote; I sometimes worry I'm just bloviating to myself in these threads.<br /> <br /> As for the B-names (since this was Blowouts day): In my outline, I had three genre suggestions: Balls, Bacchanals, and Block Parties. I didn't <i>intend </i>to have them all start with B, but I'd already called the chapter Blowouts, so I vaguely suggested to the author I assigned to roll with that theme, not expecting she'd actually come up with four more of them. Even both the sidebars start with B in that section. My only real regret is that I couldn't think of a good synonym for &quot;Genres&quot; that started with B (or at least one that wasn't a huge stretch).<br /> <br /> But yeah, the B name thing was part of an effort to take the book in a different tonal direction than the other three supplements. It's all a little sexier and funnier; not lighthearted, but like the Daeva themselves, a bit more devil-may-care.I'm particularly fond of the in-character discussion of what kind of parties the <i>other </i>clans put on, which the author really nailed in terms of snotty passive aggression.<br /> <br /> <b>Kiss of the Succubus</b> also had a more ironic tone than the other clan books, and I didn't want to lose that quality. I think we made out pretty well on that front.</div> </div> </div> </div>Devil may care is definitely a particularly favorite vein of mine for the Daeva, and I recall as I was reading (having started with Chapter 2 because my reading habits have been odd with the clan books) that this line was the one that settled me in for a good time for the rest of the evening (and I needed it at the time, I'll tellyou):<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Maybe that sounds like superstitious nonsense to you, but in my experience, superstitious nonsense doesn\u2019t give a fuck about what you think. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-17T02:55:25-08:00","id":1468107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1467058-sin-again-daeva-now-available-on-storytellers-vault-2e-requiem-clan-book?p=1468084#post1468084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My only real regret is that I couldn't think of a good synonym for &quot;Genres&quot; that started with B (or at least one that wasn't a huge stretch).</div> </div> </div> </div>*Sneaks in maliciously...*<br /> <br /> Branding?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-17T03:08:40-08:00","id":1468108,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Teatime</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1467058-sin-again-daeva-now-available-on-storytellers-vault-2e-requiem-clan-book?p=1468107#post1468107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*Sneaks in maliciously...*<br /> <br /> Branding?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I considered it! It was juuuuuuuust too far of a linguistic leap to make.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-17T05:17:42-08:00","id":1468115,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1467058-sin-again-daeva-now-available-on-storytellers-vault-2e-requiem-clan-book?p=1468108#post1468108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I considered it! It was juuuuuuuust too far of a linguistic leap to make.</div> </div> </div> </div>You could at least try in the text to talk about &quot;your brand of party&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-17T12:42:18-08:00","id":1468171,"title":"","content":"Alright, let's get into Chapter Four.<br /> <br /> <br /> ...But first, a Devotion!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sin Again: Daeva</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Speak of the Devil<br /> (Celerity \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022, Majesty \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <br /> And he shall appear. Kindred with this Devotion learn to realize this legend, seeming to always be near those thinking of them.<br /> <br /> This Devotion costs 4 Experiences to learn.<br /> <br /> <b>Cost: </b>1 Willpower<br /> <br /> <b>Requirement:</b> The victim must have been affected by the vampire\u2019s Awe within a number of nights equal to Blood Potency.<br /> <br /> <b>Dice Pool: </b>Presence + Stealth + Celerity<br /> <br /> <b>Action:</b> Instant<br /> <br /> <b>Roll Results</b><br /> <br /> <b>Success:</b> The vampire appears somewhere within the vicinity of the victim, just out of sight. If the victim speaks the vampire\u2019s name aloud within the time period noted above, she\u2019ll be aware of it, and can use this Devotion without spending a Willpower.<br /> <br /> <b>Exceptional Success: </b>The vampire is mystically aware of the surroundings she\u2019s about to appear in, and can pick up the flow of a conversation in progress, or insert herself into the scene in an otherwise dramatic fashion.<br /> <br /> <b>Failure: </b>The Blood lies still in the veins. The Devotion has no effect.<br /> <br /> <b>Dramatic Failure: </b>The vampire teleports\u2026 somewhere.</div> </div> </div> </div>Normally, I don't preview a lot of stuff from the systems chapter, but this one is one of my favourite Devotions we've ever done.<br /> <br /> Anyway, Chapter Four. Let's start with the Alu.<br /> <br /> Those of you familiar with <b>Requiem</b>'s First Edition probably remember the En, a bloodline of power-hungry Daeva who could ignore many of the downsides of diablerie due to bonding with a mysterious demon that bonds with them when they join the bloodline. The En are rather reviled among the fanbase for being able to get past a lot of the limitations of being vampires for not <i>that </i>much of a downside. I don't <i>hate </i>the En, but I do think they're kind of a period when they should be a comma. It's the difference between<br /> <br /> &quot;Join us and you can diablerize to your heart's content.&quot;<br /> <br /> and<br /> <br /> &quot;Join us and you can diablerize to your heart's content, <i>but...</i>&quot;<br /> <br /> You need that <i>but</i>, or else they're just kind of boring. Being able to do cool stuff should always come with a hefty price, at least in <b>Vampire</b>. That's drama!<br /> <br /> So, I wanted to include the En, but I felt that if we wanted to be true to their concept, they wouldn't work as a bloodline. However, they <i>would </i>work wonderfully as a Horror. So, we decided that the focus should be on that aforementioned demon. The Alu was a much more compelling catalyst for drama, and it offered a chance to make the En's diablerie proficiency into something deeply horrific.<br /> <br /> That said, we did include a short option on using them as a bloodline, and even a few plot hooks about what happened to that version of the En (if they existed at all).<br /> <br /> As for development stuff, the Alu didn't change that much through the course of production. Their Condition was initially a bit simpler, but I added a few bits and bobs from their original incarnation once final drafts were in. I also included the little sidebar from our friend &quot;M. Lucky.&quot;<br /> <br /> So, without further ado, here's the Alu/En. Tomorrow, let's look at the Nemites, new(ish) covenant.<br /> <br /> <b>Alu: The worm turns</b><br /> <br /> &quot;Ambition outlives the ambitious.&quot;<br /> <br /> <i>Newbies at Elysium are always an event.<br /> <br /> Usually, it\u2019s somebody\u2019s hot shit new childe, or another pretty young neonate who thinks she\u2019s Queen of the Damned. But last night, it was this ancilla no one\u2019s heard from in decades, apparently seeing an opportunity to start fresh. Except, the moment he sets foot in the room, Martine \u2014 d\u2019Entrement\u2019s dirty little snitch \u2014 just starts pointing and screaming at the dude like his head\u2019s spinning in its socket.<br /> <br /> No one would tell us what all the fuss was all about. We just had to sit there and wait for the goon squad to drag the poor bastard out; didn\u2019t go quietly either. Don\u2019t have the foggiest what became of him, but I doubt we\u2019ll be seeing him again any time soon.<br /> <br /> They tell me Martine never did stop screaming. Not till they staked her for the night.</i><br /> <br /> Time is an uncontested hunter. Even if a vampire never meets Final Death, the burden of her inhuman nature will eventually claim her. Tragedies beget atrocities, and atrocities beget degeneration, and degeneration begets bestiality. The Requiem is unceasing malice for the sake of survival, and the once-human mind will invariably break. The Kindred call these wretches draugr, and their vile, frenzied existences almost always meet a quick end.<br /> <br /> Almost. Once in a while, with no Humanity left to tame the Beast, something else slithers in. For as long as vampires have haunted humanity, the Alu have moved in the shadows. These bizarre creatures use draugr as meat puppets, or bargain with more humane vampires for a safe haven in return for an immense and terrible power.<br /> <br /> <b>Background</b><br /> <br /> Alu are crimson, gelatinous worms that float through Twilight. Things of spirit yet devoid of it, they have no eyes, ears, or any other sensory organs. Before it finds a host, an Alu\u2019s existence is little more than profound loneliness, punctuated by brief flashes of immense craving. If they were born with hopes or dreams, those things decay in the face of a ceaseless, deafening void.<br /> <br /> A Worm\u2019s only drive is to find a body, and to this end, the creature can sense vampires on an instinctual level. If it\u2019s lucky enough to come across a draugr, it can devour the beast\u2019s last bits of soul before taking over as the only thinking entity inside its mindless shell. There is no resistance. Once complete, this process creates a composite being: the En.<br /> <br /> But joining with a draugr is only the first step. The new En is a quick learner, eager to devour the world around it and experience all the pleasures of sight, sound, and \u2014 most of all \u2014 taste. Once it finishes digesting the last vestiges of its host\u2019s soul, a new drive coalesces. While they must sustain themselves as all vampires do, the only true meal for an En is the Amaranth, and it will bring Kindred and draugr alike to heel to sate that hunger. Vitae may fuel their stolen bodies, but they require the spark of a soul to make eternity worthwhile.<br /> <br /> Finding a draugr isn\u2019t the only way to become an En, though. It\u2019s the easiest, but vampires with no Humanity rarely survive in the All Night Society. Instead, if an Alu comes across a \u201cnormal\u201d vampire, it can try to take a willing vessel. By striking Faustian pacts, it can assure it never suffers the torment of its primordial existence again. In exchange, all the vampire has to do is commit a little diablerie now and again. And again\u2026 and again\u2026<br /> <br /> <b>En Isiratuu</b><br /> <br /> No on still living has ever witnessed an Alu\u2019s creation, and no one knows how long they live (if they have a lifespan at all). However, they do share some history.<br /> <br /> Many centuries before the fall of Rome, a city sat in the cradle of civilization. In that city, the Kindred were brash, lording over the night without the restraint of a Masquerade. The kine were their playthings, less than slaves, though there was no brotherhood among the dead. They warred on each other with such spectacle that it would make modern quarrels seem like playfighting. The Dark Strangers claim it was in this city that they first came to be, created with dark magics to aid the Kindred in their endless wars. Or perhaps they were simply opportunistic, like bacteria feeding around a festering wound.<br /> <br /> In this damned city, a monster called En Isiratuu rose as king. En was a Daeva, perhaps one of the first, and where his soul once sat, a powerful Alu guided him. He committed countless atrocities upon his people, both enemies and friends alike, for all before him was his birthright and dominion. Many tried to assuage the empty heart of their king, but all were met with failure. En could not be motivated by or pity or shame, for his cruelty existed for its own sake.<br /> <br /> Although En\u2019s kingdom fell, tonight, he\u2019s the ideal all Udug Hul aspire to. Some Kindred familiar with the myth wonder if such mastery over kine was possible at all, even in ancient times, and En\u2019s similarities to the Epic of Gilgamesh are\u2026 suspicious. But the Alu simply say that facts seem like lies to unbelievers. Joined Worms refer to themselves by En\u2019s name both in tribute and as a reminder of the heights they might achieve.<br /> <br /> <b>Body Snatching</b><br /> <br /> The presence of an En leads to disappearances of Kindred and kine alike, as many victims as the creature thinks it can get away with. The more the En eats, the more brazen it becomes, as restraint becomes unnecessary in the face of unrestrained power.<br /> <br /> Alu incursions often start when the All Night Society is at its most fractured: anywhere Kindred fight amongst themselves with enough desperation to engage in diablerie, or where draugr are left alone to fester. As crises expand beyond control, a vampire will do anything for survival, and an offer to preserve even a fraction of her power in these dire times is more than enough for Alu to get a foot in the door.<br /> <br /> With newfound strength, the Alu works to fulfill every desire and dream its host has. However, as the Worm digests each meal their bargain provides, the vampire\u2019s psyche fades away until nothing remains but a new En.<br /> <br /> <b>Systems</b><br /> <br /> Without hosts, Alu are completely vulnerable. Anyone who can physically interact with creatures in Twilight can kill an Udug Hul with a single strike, crushing it like the Worm it is. They have no traits of their own, move slowly, and aren\u2019t cognizant of the world around them beyond the presence of vampires. The one thing an Alu can sense with clarity is the taint of diablerie, which lights up like hellfire in the creature\u2019s non-vision.<br /> <br /> Whenever an Alu enters a draugr or hollows out a Kindred host\u2019s soul, the amalgamation becomes an En. Unless otherwise noted, En operate as Humanity 0 vampires, albeit ones with human intellect and an inherent diablerie addiction; they do not have clans and do not suffer acquired banes.<ul><li>The creature uses its host\u2019s traits. However, it suffers a \u20133 modifier on untrained Social Skills instead of \u20131, and failures on mundane Empathy and Socialize rolls are always dramatic. An Alu often resembles its first host\u2019s personality, sometimes even convincing itself that it\u2019s still that vampire in some way.</li> <li>With a successful diablerie, the En can choose to steal any bloodline gift the victim knows rather than a normal Discipline or Skill, if possible. It must meet any basic requirements or prerequisites to use the effect, but it can learn the power for future use. This does not allow the En to learn other powers of that bloodline, including higher dots of a unique Discipline.</li> <li>If the host body dies, the Worm is ejected into Twilight.</li> <li>If an En Embraces, it must spend a dot of Blood Potency. Its childer are always Daeva, regardless of its body\u2019s original clan.</li> <li>If it can see a vampire, an En can always sense if it has ever committed diablerie.</li> </ul><br /> If a vampire with Humanity makes a compact with a Dark Stranger, the character gains the following Condition:<br /> <br /> <b>Gifts of the Alu (Persistent)</b><br /> <br /> [REDACTED]<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-17T15:02:08-08:00","id":1468182,"title":"","content":"Out of curiosity, could you clarify at which frequency the Alu exist in (unless I missed it in the book)? While &quot;whatever fits your story&quot; works, I was just wondering which was would be more appropriate considering that the strix are Embodied entity instead of Ephemeral one so we don't have a &quot;vampire Twilight&quot;. I guess that either &quot;ghost&quot; or &quot;goetia&quot; could work, but I would like to hear your thoughts about it.<br /> <br /> Also, is M. Lucky's hints mean that we could expect the En and Alu's venomous and poisonous frenemies?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-17T15:42:34-08:00","id":1468186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1467058-sin-again-daeva-now-available-on-storytellers-vault-2e-requiem-clan-book?p=1468182#post1468182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Out of curiosity, could you clarify at which frequency the Alu exist in (unless I missed it in the book)? While &quot;whatever fits your story&quot; works, I was just wondering which was would be more appropriate considering that the strix are Embodied entity instead of Ephemeral one so we don't have a &quot;vampire Twilight&quot;. I guess that either &quot;ghost&quot; or &quot;goetia&quot; could work, but I would like to hear your thoughts about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>They exist in Twilight (I THINK that detail is in there, but I'll make absolutely sure for when I do the errata'd version). However, they're so weak that giving them stats wasn't really necessary. Basically, if need be, default to whatever the rules for creatures in Twilight are in <b>CofD</b>. They don't track any Conditions or stuff like that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, is M. Lucky's hints mean that we could expect the En and Alu's venomous and poisonous frenemies? </div> </div> </div>Perhaps! I've gone through a few ideas about how/when/where to convert the <b>Ancient Bloodlines </b>lineages. One day, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-17T15:47:34-08:00","id":1468187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1467058-sin-again-daeva-now-available-on-storytellers-vault-2e-requiem-clan-book?p=1468186#post1468186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They exist in Twilight (I THINK that detail is in there, but I'll make absolutely sure for when I do the errata'd version). However, they're so weak that giving them stats wasn't really necessary. Basically, if need be, default to whatever the rules for creatures in Twilight are in <b>CofD</b>. They don't track any Conditions or stuff like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yeah, it is stated that they exist in Twilight- but there is that concept of Twilight &quot;frequencies&quot; where entities within certain part of the Twilight can't interact with others (for example, ghosts exist in one frequency and spirits are in another, so they &quot;can't interact&quot;). Basically it breaks the Twilight into different regimes of interactions- less relevant for vampires as they barely interact with the Twilight unless they astral project themselves (which is its own frequency), so this is why I asked.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-17T16:24:44-08:00","id":1468191,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1467058-sin-again-daeva-now-available-on-storytellers-vault-2e-requiem-clan-book?p=1468187#post1468187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh yeah, it is stated that they exist in Twilight- but there is that concept of Twilight &quot;frequencies&quot; where entities within certain part of the Twilight can't interact with others (for example, ghosts exist in one frequency and spirits are in another, so they &quot;can't interact&quot;). Basically it breaks the Twilight into different regimes of interactions- less relevant for vampires as they barely interact with the Twilight unless they astral project themselves (which is its own frequency), so this is why I asked.</div> </div> </div> </div>Totally up to you. We didn't feel like the distinction would ever come up in a very meaningful way, so we didn't want to pin it down. If I HAD to choose, they're on the same frequency as ghosts, all things being equal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-18T12:45:26-08:00","id":1468294,"title":"","content":"The Nemites. Let's talk about them!<br /> <br /> For those of you who haven't read <b>The Danse Macabre</b>, the Nemites are a minor pagan covenant who worship at the altar of unconditional vampire love. They believe the love (and Vitae) of humans is sinful, a distraction from the purity of Kindred love, and they've adopted an odd syncretic cult around the worship of Diana and her herald, the Rex Nemorensis, whom they...well, <i>they </i>don't call it diablerie. But that's what it is.<br /> <br /> I've always liked the Nemites, and when I was looking at covenants we might convert for this book, they sprang out at me. They have a cool, creepy concept that's niche enough to be it's own thing, and they have a Daeva vibe that still leaves room for other clans.<br /> <br /> Originally, this covenant was going to figure into the Blowouts chapter, because I'd envisioned them having special Merits that let them be better at social gatherings: their big advantage in First Edition was people power, and that made a kind of sense to me. However, as I went on through planning, a <i>kind </i>of sense was all it really made. The problem with creating Merits for special subsystems is that if a player buys one, you either <i>have </i>to use that subsystem, or they've wasted their Experiences on something that will never come up. I don't envision the Blowout system being necessary for every chronicle (it might not even be necessary if the coterie DOES throw a party, if the stakes aren't high), so as much as that would've been aninteresting interpretation, I decided they should be a little more accessible.<br /> <br /> Our version of the Nemites doesn't differ <i>too </i>much from their original incarnation, but I think it offers a lot more modes of play, which is always my first concern. The author (Dark Days Radio host and the forum's own <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/128-dr-ether\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar128_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"128\" data-vbnamecard=\"128\">Dr Ether</a>) had the brilliant idea of adding a multi-level marketing veneer to their cult, and that gave them a focus I think the original version lacked (it also distinguished them more from the Circle of the Crone). Now the Nemites are less out and proud, but far more sinister, hiding within the other covenants and siphoning off their human resources to feed their voracious Vitae addiction. They create pyramids of vessels, keeping those at the top fed and punishing those who would sully their downline with human blood. The other big change was giving them access to Cruac, though that isn't necessarily their focus: Cruac is another way they hide themselves among the other factions (though considering &quot;the curse of the lone ritualist,&quot; one wonders just how tied to the Acolytes they truly are...)<br /> <br /> This covenant didn't change much in development. The only major addition was another Merit to reflect their First Edition Merit discount, and a little sidebar expanding on the Rex Nemorensis, which is a concept that takes a bit of work to get your head around.<br /> <br /> Anyway, that's it for me, so come on over and have a drink with the Nemites (just don't sign anything). Tomorrow, would you like to hear about a horror or a ghoul family? If no one votes, I'll decide for myself, but just know that you have the power! Also, if you haven't done so, please consider leaving us a review or a star rating on the Vault. I can't emphasize enough how useful that is to boosting sales. People often overlook community content, and a review can be a push in the right direction!<br /> <br /> <b>The Nemites: The Tree Surgeons</b><br /> <br /> &quot;Don't just maximize your downline: Bleed it dry.&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>You want to join the Nemites because</b><br /> <br /> You\u2019re looking for community. You want someone to have your back. You need to feel valued by those ahead of you and those behind you. You want to escape a stagnant Requiem within the other factions of the All Night Society. You need to rise above the rest.<br /> <br /> <b>The big picture</b><br /> <br /> Love as vampires experience it is a strange beast. Their dead hearts no longer flutter when they see a person they connect with; their bodies don\u2019t stir to have sweaty, glorious, awkward sex in one-night stands; they don\u2019t get a shot of endorphins when they see an old friend for the first time in years. They can\u2019t even mourn properly, unchanged and immortal as multitudes pass on into true death.<br /> <br /> The Nemites know this isn\u2019t real love. It\u2019s animal-like, born out of the primal needs of the ape brain. Human \u201clove\u201d is a biochemical response to sex and the need to protect offspring. Grief is also just an organic response, the lizard brain reacting to loneliness. But the love of Kindred is stronger \u2014 purer \u2014 and divorced of any built-in exchange of services, or the need to protect each other.<br /> <br /> Perhaps, they say, true love originated with the dead, wrestled from the grip of the gods. If so, the Blood isn\u2019t just a nonchemical process: It\u2019s divine.<br /> <br /> The Nemites are a cult and aspiring covenant that subscribes to the ideals of unconditional love among vampires. Through the emotional manipulations of Majesty and the binding power of Vitae, the love they build isn\u2019t a temporary bond born out of primitive need, but instead a union of a holy essence all Kindred hold within themselves, a \u201cmulti-level\u201d network of roots that nourishes their community and offers a path to spiritual ascension.<br /> <br /> Their rituals, both socially and supernaturally, form an extended network, cleaving members to each other and allowing blood to be siphoned from the bottom of their hierarchy. At the base of the tree is the Rex Nemorensis, the eternal king who subsists on this spiderweb of tributaries \u2014 one that falls apart if members break their promises. Thus, the only way to maintain this link is to trap more saplings in the system. The love of the covenant must be everything to its members, while outside connections must be cut. Permanently.<br /> <br /> <b>Where we came from</b><br /> <br /> [REDACTED]<br /> <br /> <b>Our practices</b><br /> <br /> A community is only as strong as its roots, and ours are fed with blood. Blood is an offer of freedom and an escape from stagnant power structures that would enslave Kindred for the rest of their Requiems. With us, you\u2019ll find a community that quells the Beast and soothes the loneliness of death \u2014 one with an exciting path to promotion.<br /> <br /> All kings must die, but ours is reborn in the grave, just as Kindred take their second breath with the Embrace. The title of Rex Nemorensis is claimed in a ritual combat called the Passing of the Golden Bough. Taken from our sacred grove, a branch is fashioned into a stake for a successor to drive through the reigning King\u2019s heart. Drinking deep of his Vitae and drawing his soul into theirs, the victor offers the slain monarch\u2019s blood to the community. In an orgy of gore, of entrails and bone and divine madness, the new King binds us together in an ever more perfect love. It\u2019s exhilarating. Enlightening. Something we all crave, leading us all to seek the Bough. As a final act, the new Rex Nemorensis rips the spine from the former, planting it in the sacred grove as a symbolic green shoot.<br /> <br /> Like Hippolytus, we server ties to mortal desires that would bind us to a profane world, and which would dilute our downlines. Our love is founded on true, sanguine devotion \u2014 what other vampires crudely call the Vinculum. But ours is no involuntary bondage as that awful word suggests: We are a family formed by the purest <i>agape</i>.<br /> <br /> Each Nemite is expected to tend to their downline. Some run self-help groups, others mentor investors through mindfulness training. The goal is same: Be a good influencer, keep up the engagement of prospects, and crush mortal distractions. No, no, it\u2019s not so oppressive as it sounds! This is community building. This is working together for the benefit of the Upstream, and sometimes that means acting for the good of all rather than the good of you.<br /> <br /> You too can benefit from our growing and dynamic community. You too can be a sponsor! But just how do we spread our message to the masses? \u201cTo grow out roots, we must recruit!\u201d We silently exist within the other covenants, mimicking a dynastic house, or a Dragon chantry, or even a Carthian cell. Our veneration of the reborn king nestles within the Lancea et Sanctum\u2019s teachings just as well as it does within the Circle of the Crone\u2019s. Hidden in plain sight, we identify those who\u2019ve been trampled by the humanist sects and offer them a path out. Acolytes are the easiest marks, as our rituals and blood sorcery closely follow those taught by the Dark Mother.<br /> <br /> Conflict comes between our family and the Circle when, like a weed, we grow too wild and deep within their garden. They see us as usurpers, enforcing a lockstep faith, but we don\u2019t seek to drown out their choir. We just want to create harmony. It\u2019s a shame some wish to sing their own song so selfishly. Such singular voices must be stifled, and if doing so adds to the Upstream? Well, at least they found a way to make a contribution.<br /> <br /> Care must be taken to maintain our downline, but feeding upon mortals is profane, opening our divine souls to sin. Drinking human blood pleasures the Beast and drives us to dark temptations. Yet, as keepers of Hecate\u2019s faith, we stand at the crossroads of life and death, and for this we must balance the scales. Just as we transmute blood into Vitae, death into life, we cleanse the world of sin as we suckle on the blood of man. And so, our faith is a paradox: We strive for purity while tainting ourselves with mortal sin. However, the act of gifting blood to others \u2014 watering the roots of our society \u2014 balances the scales as our love transforms the polluted blood of mortals. Therefore, each night we gather, our downline presenting kine as offerings to the family, and we collectively feed. Share the sin, save the sinners.<br /> <br /> However, there are limits to that principle. When the roots break down, when the downline fails, there must be reparations, and those who violate our family\u2019s faith must balance the scales. Just as the Rex Nemorensis must water the roots with their passing, so too must the penitent make sacrifice: One of their mortal blood relatives must be offered up in a symbolic act of severing their connection to the profane world.<br /> <br /> We count all clans within our number, and each one has guided our tree at different times through history \u2014 even (allegedly) the Julii in our earliest nights. However, of all the Kindred, those of Daeva blood tend to stand at the forefront of our community. The nature of the Serpents\u2019 curse means our teachings have great benefit to them. Coupled with their command of mortal hearts, they quickly master the downline and spread our roots far and wide.<br /> <br /> Speaking of, how about we get you signed up?<br /> <br /> <b>New Merits (Excerpt)<br /> <br /> Community Chest (\u2022)</b><br /> <br /> <b>Prerequisite:</b> Nemite Status \u2022<br /> <br /> <b>Effect: </b>A community is defined by its members. Maybe that\u2019s a truism, but the Tree Surgeons martial their personal connections almost to the exclusion of all other assets. As such, they always have backup. Your character gains access to dots in Allies, Contacts, Mentor, and Retainer equal to Covenant Status, distributed as you see fit. This benefit applies to Status in all covenants. For example, if she has three dots with the Nemites and one with the Carthians, she gains four dots of these Social Merits.<br /> <br /> <b>Drawback: </b>These resources belong to the Grove, and drawing on them for selfish purposes is bad for the Upstream. Furthermore, if your character is accessing another covenant\u2019s social resources, she\u2019d better be willing to share them with her real family when times get tough.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-18T13:37:27-08:00","id":1468297,"title":"","content":"So with the Nemites hiding among covenants and members of the Legion from False Gods hiding among covenants, does it mean we have a vampire spy game? I can really imagine them both trying to frame each other from their own crimes while trying to avoid drawing attention for themselves, or even just use &quot;VII paranoia&quot; while they fight each other for control.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-18T16:54:32-08:00","id":1468308,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1467058-sin-again-daeva-now-available-on-storytellers-vault-2e-requiem-clan-book?p=1468294#post1468294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We count all clans within our number, and each one has guided our tree at different times through history \u2014 <i>even (allegedly) the Julii in our earliest nights</i>. However, of all the Kindred, those of Daeva blood tend to stand at the forefront of our community. The nature of the Serpents\u2019 curse means our teachings have great benefit to them. Coupled with their command of mortal hearts, they quickly master the downline and spread our roots far and wide.</div> </div> </div> </div>This particular bit got my mental gears spinning in a number of ways.<br /> <br /> How old the Nemites practice truly are, could they harken to something older than roman or greek deities?<br /> Are the Julii the only dead clan to leave marks in the cycle of death and renewal that empowers their entangled bloody family tree?<br /> Could horrors not quite kindred but somewhat similar to the daeva like the Cihuateteo or Gh\u00fcls relate somehow to their past sins or tainted offerings of kine?<br /> How do Mandragora or Lacrima fit in the purified stream that flows toward the roots?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-18T17:21:29-08:00","id":1468313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1467058-sin-again-daeva-now-available-on-storytellers-vault-2e-requiem-clan-book?p=1468308#post1468308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This particular bit got my mental gears spinning in a number of ways.<br /> <br /> How old the Nemites practice truly are, could they harken to something older than roman or greek deities?<br /> Are the Julii the only dead clan to leave marks in the cycle of death and renewal that empowers their entangled bloody family tree?<br /> Could horrors not quite kindred but somewhat similar to the daeva like the Cihuateteo or Gh\u00fcls relate somehow to their past sins or tainted offerings of kine?<br /> How do Mandragora or Lacrima fit in the purified stream that flows toward the roots?</div> </div> </div> </div>Diana/Artemis is a very old deity. I wouldn't be surprised if she had predecessor cults. If, of course, the Nemites are truthful about their ancient lineage. But if they aren't, why do their &quot;roots&quot; work at all?<br /> <br /> Well, we may be hearing more from the Nemites in [REDACTED], which might be in a good position to provide some historical clues...<br /> <br /> As for Mandragora, the Nemites ABSOLUTELY use them. They probably know more about them than even the Crone (this is something I considered adding in development, but I just didn't have the room).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":192,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","user":"Yossarian","date":". 11-18-2021, 08:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-19T00:48:28-08:00","id":1468335,"title":"","content":"Small nitpick: En isn't a name. It's a title. The Alus don't take Isiratuu's name as a tribute; they take his title as their name.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-19T18:35:50-08:00","id":1468377,"title":"","content":"Hello! Sorry for the radio silence today! I was out and about, and it took much more time than I thought it would. I'm a bit wiped right now, so I'm going to save our next excerpt for tomorrow. I might even make it a twofer if I've got some time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-20T13:04:48-08:00","id":1468418,"title":"","content":"Welcome back! Let's look at a ghoul family.<br /> <br /> The Children of Nirriti are from all the way back in the original <b>Ghouls </b>sourcebook. Those of you who've followed these threads of mine probably know that I have a complicated relationship with <b>Ghouls</b>. There's some really good stuff in there, but it's also offensive and puerile in a way that really tests one's patience. The 1E Children definitely fall on the puerile side of <b>Ghouls</b>. They're also pretty boring. They did bad things to make their very-specific-backstory master feel good about herself, and generally had a lot of sex and performed a lot of masochism.<br /> <br /> This is one of the few instances in our updates where we've just done away with the backstory altogether. Normally, I try to preserve at least a seed of it, but my brief for the author was to use the name and some of the trappings, but to otherwise jettison the rest. If you squint, you could probably fit the old backstory in, but we didn't feel anyone would miss it all that much. And, as always, if you like the old version, you can always use that in conjunction without our updated systems.<br /> <br /> The 2E Children of Nirriti take the original's vague sin-eater concept and puts it to the forefront: these are ghouls who can feed on a vampire's blood and lessen her curse, in exchange for giving her the ability to perform higher levels of Cruac (normally ghouls can only do level one rites). In terms of development, the only really big addition was a sidebar about the Nemites, who fit very well together with our version of the Nirriti Cult.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I'll let the write-up speak for itself. Tomorrow, I'm going to take a break, because I need to catch up on some housework, but on Monday, we'll have a look at another ghoul family: the Brigmans.<br /> <br /> <b>Children of Nirriti: The ones who pray for you</b><br /> <br /> &quot;O Goddess! Invest thy sin in me!&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>Where we came from</b><br /> <br /> In the beginning there was chaos. Then, the goddess Nirriti granted humanity the sanctity of death. With a final stop, she gave the confusion of living a destination and a purpose, and in return for worship, so say her Children, the goddess provides them the power to keep disorder at bay.<br /> <br /> The Children of Nirriti sprang up in India in the waning nights of the colonial age. Perhaps they were once true worshippers of the Vedic goddess, but if so, that hasn\u2019t been true as long as anyone living or dead can remember. The self-proclaimed Chosen are one of the most fervent ghoul cults in the All Night Society, and the Serpents own them body and soul. The Daeva wouldn\u2019t allow it otherwise. By taking Vitae from their patrons, these ghouls \u201ceat\u201d Kindred sins for a short time, lessening the Curse.<br /> <br /> Where they acquired this trait is unknown. The party line, of course, is that the goddess Nirriti blessed them to work her will, infusing their blood with the ability to leech chaos from the world. For their part, the Daeva believe this deity was one of their own, some Serpent who was clever enough to appropriate a goddess of death as her disguise. This doesn\u2019t answer the question of how she imbued her servants with a way to mitigate her bane, but perhaps her assumed identity became more than a mask.<br /> <br /> If Nirriti was just another Serpent with a god complex, she could\u2019ve done worse than styling herself after a Vedic god, one with so many names to hide behind. Any vampire of any gender can wear the mantle of \u201cNirriti\u201d and gain a dedicated coven, just as long as they\u2019re willing to suffer (or indulge) in the cult\u2019s theology. To the Chosen, Kindred are gods who walk among the living. With their own Mistress of Death watching over them, smiting their enemies and granting them boons, the Sin-Eaters accept every twist of fate and feeding as divinely ordained. They believe they bleed the taint of a fallen world by accepting its burden from their goddess. Perhaps their rituals only stem the tide, but eating a little chaos is better than allowing the void on the edges of reality to claw its way in.<br /> <br /> <b>Who we are tonight</b><br /> <br /> The Chosen are no longer recluses in saffron robes and isolated temples. Perhaps you\u2019ve even met one and not known it: Sin-Eaters work their rituals around unassuming jobs and in quiet suburbs, or concentrate their operations in \u201cchaotic\u201d regions where wars, disease, and decay flourish. There\u2019s no better way to keep the madness at bay than to wade through it.<br /> <br /> Some Nirriti cults still hold to the old Vedic litanies, but others have transmuted their practices into the Wiccan, Pagan, Santer\u00edan, or even secular Satanist traditions. While Sin-Eaters can be found all across the All Night Society, they\u2019re most often tied to Serpents in the Circle of the Crone and (more and more of late) the Nemites, as most of the family\u2019s teachings center around the practice of blood magic.<br /> <br /> However, even outside the auspices of the Mother\u2019s Army or the Tree Surgeons, the family practices Cr\u00faac as a sacrament for their deity and as a practical way to punish sin. As the Chosen send more of their scions into the world, they prove themselves devoted additions to all the other Kindred covenants. A few are even associated with the Lancea et Sanctum; it\u2019s no great leap from pagan sacrifices of body and blood to the pomp and ceremony of a Black Mass. Sanctified Chosen and their regnants are careful not to flaunt the family\u2019s Cr\u00faac use, but many justify it as the cost of fighting sin. Sometimes you beat the Devil by using his own tools against him.<br /> <br /> The forms of sin include betrayals of their blood kin or profane acts against their particular version of the faith, or at least their regnant\u2019s interpretation if it. All relationships and pregnancies are strictly controlled by the High Priests and Priestesses of each branch of the family, and all is done in service to the Goddess of Death, for without her they cannot hold the void at bay forever.<br /> <br /> This is the role of the Children of Nirriti \u2014 but what do they do when the goddess defies their traditions? The Chosen don\u2019t worship Kindred idly; they expect their deities to uphold their duties, smiting the family\u2019s rivals and providing them the Vitae required for their rites. The vampire who abuses her Chosen, who wallows in sin and allows chaos to reign, will find her ghouls\u2019 magic turned against her. When a false divinity abandons her followers, her flock may rise up and perform a final ritual, consuming their goddess whole and raising another, better one in her place.<br /> <br /> <b>Benefit: </b>Once per week, if a vampire feeds Vitae to a Sin-Eater in a special ritual, her Humanity is considered one dot higher for the purposes of all acquired banes, to a limit of ten. If she\u2019s a Daeva, it\u2019s two dots. This lasts until she suffers her next breaking point or a week passes, whichever comes first. In addition, while bearing a vampire\u2019s sinful Vitae, a Chosen ghoul\u2019s own blood is sufficient for sacrifices in Cr\u00faac rites higher than the first level. However, unless she can store enough Vitae to cover the rite\u2019s entire cost, she must inflict herself with lethal damage for each Vitae in excess of her reserves, or share costs with other sin-bearing Children.<br /> <br /> <b>Drawback:</b> [REDACTED]<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-21T13:27:26-08:00","id":1468521,"title":"","content":"Quick note as a duck my head in from cleaning up my house: I just implemented a bunch of a errata, so if you've purchased the pdf, version 2.0 is ready for download. Mostly it's typos and the like, but there are a few small mechanics fixes; mostly just clarifying what things are supposed to do. As always, if you like the book, please consider leaving us a review, or just a star rating! It's so helpful, and you'll have the Daeva's eternal gratitude (if you're into that sort of thing).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-22T13:15:45-08:00","id":1468628,"title":"","content":"A good Monday to you all! Let's talk about the Brigmans.<br /> <br /> In a technical sense, the Brigmans are a First Edition ghoul family, but they never had any mechanics, or even much of an existence outside of their regnant, Solomon Birch, the signature Daeva character. In a nutshell, the family is Birch's attempt to breed a race of perfect humans who could deny the temptations of vampires and lead the rest of humanity to God's holy light. They get a few name-checks throughout various sourcebooks, including the three Chicago <b>Requiem </b>novels (or, well, two of them). Even then, their origins aren't all that concrete. The most we get about them specifically is in <b>Night Horrors: Immortal Sinners</b>, where Birch is detailed as a potential antagonist.<br /> <br /> Originally, I didn't plan on doing the Brigmans, partly because I didn't even remember they existed. I was going to do the Children of Nirriti, and the author who ended up doing <i>them </i>was going to do another new one. However, as one does, I fell down a rabbit hole of <b>Requiem </b>lore. I was also trying to shoehorn in an update to Birch's stats in <b>Immortal Sinners</b>, and putting some numbers on his horrifying ghoul family was a good place for it, especially as a way to talk about Birch in the context of the 2E Daeva bane. This was part of the reason we have four ghoul families in the book as opposed to the usual three. I didn't want to have the lore-heavy ghoul family take up the space of one you can plug into any setting. Not that you couldn't transplant Birch and the Brigmans (or just the Brigmans) into another setting, but I like to make sure readers get as much bang for their buck as possible.<br /> <br /> The Brigmans also presented a chance to emphasize the Daeva's physical side. It's easy to lean on the social aspects of the Serpents, but that Celerity + Vigor combo packs a nasty punch. Birch also famously had no Majesty, so that was another reason to make them a bit burly.<br /> <br /> This family <i>also </i>gave me an opportunity to expand on just a <i>smidge </i>of setting detail from <b>Chicago</b>. One of the sample characters is featured in <i>The Marriage of Virtue and Viciousness</i>, and to my knowledge, her fate was never revealed (apart from a minor mention in <b>Vampire: The Requiem for Dummies</b>, of all things). If you're a fan of the Chicago novels, that's my little treat for you.<br /> <br /> So, let's meet the Brigmans. Tomorrow, let's set the ghouls aside for a moment and look at another antagonist: The Flowers of Innana.<br /> <br /> <b>Brigman: The ones who stand above you</b><br /> <br /> &quot;Mercy? No. If God needed you alive, you would\u2019ve won.'<br /> <br /> <b>Where we came from</b><br /> <br /> Let it never be said that Solomon Birch takes half measures. Like all good Sanctified, Chicago\u2019s Black Bishop believes vampires are a race of Devil\u2019s Advocates, one that tests the faithful and takes the sinful as payment. Still (and not to question God\u2019s plan) it\u2019s not the most efficient system. Not all vampires adhere to the Longinian creed, and most don\u2019t care about the difference between sacred and profane feeding. This troubles Birch. It\u2019s a contradiction in the Almighty\u2019s perfect order. Or rather, it <i>seems </i>like one. But God can\u2019t make mistakes, so that means it\u2019s a riddle to solve \u2014 and Birch thinks he\u2019s found an answer.<br /> <br /> Enter the Brigmans. They are the Elect, a beacon that will one day guide humanity against the darkness of the Kindred race, injecting true holiness into the flock so the wolves won\u2019t be necessary. Maybe that skirts some Christian dogma, but Solomon Birch is no Christian.<br /> <br /> The Brigmans were a fixture in Chicago\u2019s upper crust long before Birch got his golden claws in them. They invested early in the city\u2019s vast infrastructure, making a fortune with Brigman Transport, Inc., and this simple fact attracted Birch in his salad night. He needed the cash, and he had a Serpent\u2019s lust for the family\u2019s beautiful (married) daughter, Elena. He\u2019ll say now that he was drawn to them due to the purity of their bloodline, but just how he came around to this understanding is obscure, and Birch isn\u2019t one to show his work.<br /> <br /> Some loose tongues at Elysium say Elena refused his Vitae when he first tried to court her; others joke she slapped him for getting fresh. Whatever the catalyst, Birch found a spark in his ghoul that coalesced into a Requiem\u2019s work. The Black Bishop is no geneticist, but he is a craftsman, and he believes he can apply his artistry to the human genome in ways secular scientists don\u2019t have the imagination to conceive.<br /> <br /> Of course, the problem with eugenics, apart from being a pretty clearcut example of evil, is that they\u2019re nonsense. Birch might argue his blood makes the difference, and that mortal genetics have little to do with his project beyond metaphor, but when has Vitae done anything but twist the human soul into more contorted shapes?<br /> <br /> That\u2019s a question he\u2019s not prepared to answer. No matter how hard he pretends otherwise, Birch\u2019s fixation on humanity is just as potent as any other Serpent\u2019s, and he\u2019s as dependent on the Brigmans as they are on him. All he\u2019s managed to do is remake the Elect in his own image, and one night, they may be unlucky enough for him to realize it.<br /> <br /> <b>Who we are tonight</b><br /> <br /> The Brigmans are a family in the organized crime mold, albeit with fundamentalist vampires cooking the books instead of gangsters. Like the mafia, not all are directly related, but they\u2019ve all tasted the Black Bishop\u2019s Vitae, and that\u2019s more than enough to make you Elect. Their internal structure is stringent yet ever-shifting, with different factions vying for power and Kindred favor. A few things are set in stone, though: The dead are better than the living; the living are less than Brigmans.<br /> <br /> Wherever Birch extends his influence, the Elect are on the vanguard with money and muscle, but that doesn\u2019t mean their service is exclusive. In recent years, Birch has allowed a degree of autonomy as long as they keep the faith, so Brigmans can be both hired help and guns for rent. Every last one of them is bound to him, so it doesn\u2019t really matter how much sinful Kindred blood gets in their veins. Plus, it\u2019s good to throw some new DNA in the gene pool from time to time. It\u2019s also good for his donation plate, and the Brigmans provide soft power to a Lick known mostly for the lash.<br /> <br /> The Elect specialize in anything that requires muscle. Often, that\u2019s taking a baseball bat to some lowlife\u2019s knees, but these ghouls weren\u2019t bred just to be goons. Their construction company front is a good way to access their brawn, but sometimes the appearance of strength is useful too. If you have the cachet to enter a meeting flanked by Solomon Fucking Birch\u2019s brutes, it says a lot about the direction your Requiem is taking.<br /> <br /> The other reason he rents them out is to breed resentment. Seeing the depravity of other Kindred firsthand, yet having to bow to them, isn\u2019t great for the superiority complex Birch has bred into them. That\u2019s the point. One night, he wants them to betray him; not just to quietly disobey when they think he\u2019ll never find out (he always does), but to aim a stake at his vile heart. If the Brigmans are Elect in truth and not just name, they need to break his grasp. Only then can they make the Kindred obsolete. With each generation, a defiance burns in them like flame working through a taper. When the wick is ash, Birch will know if it was all worth it.<br /> <br /> <b>Benefit:</b> The Black Bishop has spent decades molding his Elect into Godly beings, and while his plan is far from complete, he\u2019s produced some interesting specimens in the meantime. Brigmans gain three additional dots at character creation to spend on Physical Merits. In addition, due to their regnant\u2019s spurning of his clan Discipline, few Brigmans know any Majesty. Instead, they gain access to Dominate.<br /> <br /> <b>Drawback:</b> [REDACTED]","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":192,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","user":"Yossarian","date":". 11-23-2021, 06:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-23T16:11:21-08:00","id":1468712,"title":"","content":"Let's dig up the Flowers of Inanna!<br /> <br /> The Flowers are humans who've suffered a vampire's feeding and come back different. Claiming to be blessed by a primordial goddess, they return from near death to sap away Kindred Blood Potency in exchange for immortality.<br /> <br /> I don't have much to say regarding development of this one, really (I also accidentally deleted my post draft, so I don't feel like rewriting all of it!) Mostly, the changes to the Flowers were about making them more player-friendly and more efficient. For the former, I made their Afterglow period into a Supernatural Tolerance Trait, similar to Magnitude and similar traits for other mortal(ish) monsters; I could picture them in <b>Hunter </b>chronicles, or even as allies for vampires. For the latter, I cut some details about them producing dhampir more easily from sexual encounters with Kindred. It wasn't a <i>bad </i>idea, but it felt rather redundant with material in <b>Half-Damned</b>, and it was honestly one too many things for an already system-heavy character type.<br /> <br /> Enjoy the excerpt! Tomorrow, I'll be back with one of our more abstract &quot;antagonists&quot;: Solace.<br /> <br /> <b>Flowers of Inanna: Love's labors revenged</b><br /> <br /> &quot;Is this real? Well, tonight it is.&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>AKA: Ishtari, Astarte\u2019s Tears</b><br /> <br /> She\u2019s watching you. She has been since you walked in the club. She\u2019s not your normal type, but she\u2019s got something about her that feels just right for tonight. And maybe tomorrow night. You planned your evening around a quick hookup and a meal, but you just can\u2019t get her out of your head. Maybe it\u2019s something genuine for once. Maybe\u2026<br /> <br /> Or maybe you\u2019re being played.<br /> <br /> The Daeva are nothing if not arrogant, but perhaps they\u2019ve earned the right. They have the power to create city-spanning herds and are endowed with a Kiss with pleasures deeper than any orgasm. It\u2019s only natural that these Kindred would attract their fair share of hangers-on and stalkers. But hidden among that clinging throng is something vampires so rarely encounter: predators.<br /> <br /> <b>Background</b><br /> <br /> The Flowers of Inanna say they\u2019re blessed by a scornful goddess, one with an endless hunger for the pleasures of dead flesh. By playing at being mere victims and blood dolls, the Ishtari worm their way into the All Night Society, providing potent pleasures for even the most jaded Lick. To love one of the Flowers is to know (an approximation of) true love, but such joy carries a steep price, one they\u2019re ordained to collect. Each caress thins a vampire\u2019s blood a little more, and eventually, it leaves her a helpless whelp.<br /> <br /> <b>The Queen of Heaven</b><br /> <br /> As their name suggests, the Flowers trace their origins to Inanna (sometimes called Ishtar, or Astarte, or even Athena), the Mesopotamian Queen of Heaven. Inanna was a greedy and spiteful creature, known for her many attempts to steal power from other divine beings. According to legend, one day, she decided to conquer the underworld, the domain of her sister, Ereshkihal. However, when she stood before the gates demanding entry, Ereshkihal struck her dead for the blasphemy, for the living can never enter death\u2019s domain. Of course, gods can\u2019t truly die, and even in death, Inanna still lusted for power. So, Ereshkihal hung her sister\u2019s body on a hook to suffer the fate of living death for all time.<br /> <br /> As Inanna hung on that hook, she was visited by Nergal, her sister\u2019s husband and Lord of Death. The two had long lusted for each other, and so in death they consummated their desire. Three times he went to her, and each time he whispered a grand promise: he would free her; he would abandon his wife for her; he would give her the underworld as her kingdom. And three times he abandoned her as the morning came, left to hang on the hook.<br /> <br /> When her father\u2019s servants finally came to free her from this mess of her own creation, Inanna returned to her heavenly throne, wiser but more vindictive than ever. She had heard the promises of the dead and now knew the lies behind their pretty words. And so, Inanna took the seed Nergal left within her and sowed it within the souls of mortals, ones who had suffered the touch of the death as well, and blessed them with a divine purpose.<br /> <br /> <b>Justice from Above</b><br /> <br /> Every Ishtari has been the victim of vampiric violation, and all bear scars of their encounter, be they psychological or physical. The Flowers believe their suffering calls out to Inanna and her own experiences in the underworld, and that their goddess helps them balance the scales. Whenever a mortal is afflicted by a vampire\u2019s bite, there\u2019s a small chance they\u2019ll be visited by a vision of a beautiful woman radiating warmth and life. These visitations are most common among feeding victims close to death, as the proximity to the underworld is said to draw Inanna\u2019s attention. When the being appears, she offers the victim a choice between a gentle, kind death or a long life filled with power \u2014 and justice.<br /> <br /> If he accepts, the new Flower awakens bearing the Mark of Inanna, an eight-pointed rose symbol that resembles a tattoo. The Mark grows as the Ishtari ages, spreading vines across his skin. With each Kindred victim left in his wake, a thorn sprouts along the snaking vine, and legend has it the oldest Ishtari have marks that spread over every inch of exposed flesh.<br /> <br /> <b>Necromance</b><br /> <br /> An Ishtari\u2019s presence is invariably captivating to Kindred, and her touch is as addictive as any narcotic. However, these encounters come with a price to the victim: the potency of their blood. By leeching a vampire\u2019s death energies, a Flower can prolong her own life, revitalizing her body and gaining access to immense reserves of strength and will.<br /> <br /> To prey on their victims, Flowers masquerade as blood dolls and groupies, or even cultists if they know where to look. In particular, their ability to shrug off Majesty allows them to pass freely through Daeva circles where a normal mortal would find himself ensnared, entranced, or dead.<br /> <br /> An Ishtari is indistinguishable from a normal human in all ways except one: Her presence is intoxicating to Kindred. This passion isn\u2019t one-sided, though. As an Ishtari makes her way into the All Night Society, she begins to feel a sympathy for the dead. Most Flowers are aware of the threat their affection presents their lovers, but the connection need not be hostile. Many choose not to share the truth of their nature, but it\u2019s as often for fear of abandonment as it is for their own safety. Perhaps the most damning gift of all is not that the Flowers of Inanna must feed upon the curse of vampirism, but that they\u2019re fated to love the ones they devour.<br /> <br /> <b>Systems</b><br /> <br /> The Flowers of Inanna enjoy several inherent powers, as well as abilities granted by the <i>Afterglow</i>, the period where their bodies digest the power borrowed from their Kindred victims.<br /> <br /> <b>Innate Powers</b><br /> <br /> The Queen of Heaven\u2019s blessing provides the following traits:<br /> <br /> <b>Allure</b><br /> <br /> By spending a Willpower, an Ishtari can make sure she stands out in a crowd. For the rest of the night, if she falls within the range of a vampire\u2019s Kindred Senses, he gains the Swooning Condition toward her. To resist, his player can spend a Willpower and roll Resolve + Blood Potency vs. Presence + Manipulation + Afterglow. If he prevails, he\u2019s immune to the Ishtari\u2019s charm for the scene, or the night if it\u2019s an exceptional success.<br /> <br /> <b>Death Sight</b><br /> <br /> All Flowers gain Unseen Sense: Kindred. In addition, with a Wits + Occult + Afterglow roll, an Ishtari character can learn a vampire\u2019s rough Blood Potency. On a success, the Storyteller must reveal if the trait is greater than one (if it\u2019s five or less) or greater than five (if it\u2019s six or more).<br /> <br /> Flowers of Inanna can identify Daeva on sight, and any other clans they\u2019ve fed from before.<br /> <br /> <b>Emotional Control</b><br /> <br /> Ishtari are immune to blood bonds, and they cannot be Embraced or turned into ghouls. They are also resistant to the Kiss and the Assault, though they can still find the Kiss pleasurable. Furthermore, as an instant action, a Flower can choose to dismiss Majesty effects if they apply to her, ending (but not resolving) any relevant Conditions. However, for each scene she allows the Discipline\u2019s effects to stand, she refreshes a Willpower.<br /> <br /> <b>Feeding</b><br /> <br /> Once a night, if a vampire spends more than a few minutes in skin-to-skin contact with an Ishtari, he temporarily loses a Blood Potency dot, refreshes a spent Willpower, and gains the Half Dead Condition. If he has the Swooning Condition toward her, it resolves and becomes Dependent, which fades when he restores all Blood Potency; if he can avoid contact for a full 24 hours, dots start to return at a rate of one every (Humanity) nights. If further trysts would reduce Blood Potency to zero, he instead gains the persistent form of Half Dead and refreshes all Willpower.<br /> Such connections rarely run one-way. When a Flower drains a Blood Potency, her player can choose to accept the Swooning Condition for a Beat, but only if she doesn\u2019t have it toward the vampire already.<br /> <br /> A Flower can suppress her feeding effect until dawn, but it costs a Willpower to reactivate it. She cannot feed on vampires in daysleep or torpor.<br /> <br /> <b>Half Dead (Persistent)</b><br /> <br /> [REDACTED]<br /> <br /> <b>Afterglow</b><br /> <br /> [REDACTED]","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":192,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","user":"Yossarian","date":". 11-24-2021, 02:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-23T16:39:47-08:00","id":1468713,"title":"","content":"The Flowers are pretty interesting! As friend or foe, they seem to work very well for Vampire chronicles, even ones without a Daeva among the PCs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27083-truemrmultiverse","name":"TrueMrMultiverse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27083_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-24T07:33:54-08:00","id":1468756,"title":"","content":"Just loved them. Seriously, loved them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-24T15:47:00-08:00","id":1468789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1467058-sin-again-daeva-now-available-on-storytellers-vault-2e-requiem-clan-book?p=1468756#post1468756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just loved them. Seriously, loved them.</div> </div> </div> </div>That IS what they want you to do. &gt;_&gt;<br /> <br /> Anyway, let's pass around some Solace.<br /> <br /> This is going to be another short dev note, as updating Solace came pretty easily to me, and it didn't see a lot of changes once the first draft was finished. The big change, as noted above, was that it was originally going to tie in with the Erzs\u00e9bet bloodline. I had this whole multiple-choice backstory of how it related to them, and it just...didn't work. It wouldn't have hurt the Cavaliers to have a connection to Solace, but I don't think the reverse is true. Plus, what I had made the S a little too definite, even if the backstories were optional. Solace works best as something that's a little unknowable, and I think the write-up I ended up with maintains that obscurity without making it opaque. In any case, I was able to appropriate a lot of that material from my Erzs\u00e9bet version for the final one. It's always nice to have half the work done already.<br /> <br /> Originally, Solace appeared in <b>Mythologies</b>, and the mechanics there are...complex. However, I did appropriate the idea of it having a purity rating from that. Otherwise, it's fairly mechanics light. As for what it really is, I <i>feel </i>like that's been revealed in other books if you read between the lines (I'm pretty sure Rose even said it outright somewhere), but I wanted to maintain some ambiguity for this. I'm especially fond of the final rumor I included...<br /> <br /> So, here's Solace. Tomorrow, being Thanksgiving, I think we'll focus on a (ghoul) family: The Tribute Society.<br /> <br /> <b>Solace: Liquid nostalgia</b><br /> <br /> &quot;First taste's free.&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>Background</b><br /> <br /> The Sanctified call it sin. The Carthians say it\u2019s bourgeois decadence. The Invictus want to market it. The Ordo Dracul are performing clinical trials. And the Acolytes? They\u2019ll burn every last syrette given the chance.<br /> <br /> Solace (<b>Vampire: The Requiem</b>, p. 73) is a drug that provides Kindred with a day of pseudo-mortality. This effect is akin to the blush of life, but the feeling is far more intense, and it comes with a spiritual sense of wholeness. That\u2019s as much as anyone knows for sure; those who claim otherwise are just repeating hearsay and folklore.<br /> <br /> The S is rare enough that when it does show up in a domain, it\u2019s usually only for a few hours. If a dealer\u2019s stock lasts even a night, it\u2019s notable. From a practical standpoint, its rarity means it\u2019s not exactly habit forming, but if you\u2019ve done a hit even once, you\u2019ll never want to miss another chance.<br /> <br /> Serpents are especially vulnerable to Solace addiction; it\u2019s an easy way for them to indulge both their narcissism and their humanity habit. Daeva high on the S can <i>almost </i>convince themselves they\u2019re not just wolves among sheep. The idea that mortality could be a needle prick away is thrilling, and many Serpents are willing to forget it\u2019s an obvious lie as long as it\u2019s a soothing one. The prince gets to play pauper for a day, and when the sun falls and his blood turns blue again, he goes back to his velvet-lined coffin convinced he\u2019s learned something.<br /> <br /> It never remains so comfortable. Getting hooked on Solace is like being addicted to a dream, something that\u2019s real and clear and true for a moment, then cloudy like a cataract in the light of day. Indeed, trying to reclaim that high is a great way to meet the sun. The worst S addicts crave the warmth of sunlight as much as that sweet pinch beneath their tongues. When they lose their supplies, they play chicken with the dawn, hoping to spark something other than fourth-degree burns.<br /> <br /> <b>Hearsay</b><br /> <br /> As for what it is, no one with that information is willing to share it. One rumor suggests Solace is distilled from the blood of women who commit self-harm, though every vampire who\u2019s tried to prove that theory has come away with little more than intense shame. Some Dragon biologists say it\u2019s the blood of Inamorata, beings who resemble a vampire\u2019s long-lost mortal lover. Drinking Vitae from Inamorata has a similar effect to the drug, but these strange creatures are far rarer than even Solace, and highly individual. A similar theory ties it to the Flowers of Inanna (p. 134), but the Ishtari consider it their one true bane, disdaining its presence in a vampire\u2019s blood. A few fundamentalist Sanctified say it\u2019s the work of the Devil, and that, somewhere, Satanists are bottling the blood and tears of seventh sons to tempt Kindred into the Adversary\u2019s arms.<br /> <br /> The only consistent rumor states that the drug has something to do with blood, and this at least holds the weight of evidence. A hit of Solace provides a bit of Vitae, and it\u2019s hard not to speculate on who bled for it. As a general rule, vampires are pretty cool with bloodletting, but how much varies from Lick to Lick. Maybe a lot more Kindred hold the truth about Solace than they let on, and the reason they keep it obscured is because of the hunt that would inevitably follow its unveiling. Or maybe they just don\u2019t want competition.<br /> <br /> <b>Folklore</b><br /> <br /> Tracking the history of Solace is as byzantine as finding its source. Needle drugs didn\u2019t exist until the 19th century, yet fragmentary tales mention similar potions as far back as the Camarilla, sometimes calling it Ambrosia or Manna, or any other host of divine food. However, these anecdotes never really form a cohesive narrative, and most are poetic to the point of obscurity. Some might just be talking about plain old opium.<br /> <br /> Most Kindred believe Solace is a modern phenomenon, or at least that its increased availability is. Not that you can find it on any street corner, but the S is more common tonight than even a decade ago, still dismissed as myth in some corners of the All Night Society, but spreading further and further with every year.<br /> <br /> <b>Rumors (Excerpt)</b><br /> <br /> <i>\u201cIt\u2019s the Dracul. Evidence? It\u2019s always the Dracul.\u201d</i><br /> <br /> It\u2019s not the Dragons. Definitely, probably not. It\u2019s not Dracula either. Dracula bottling his blood? Come on. Dracula bottling his blood and creating thousands of Vincula interlinked through the Coil of the Voivode? Wow. Got any spare tinfoil hats? Don\u2019t let anyone catch you spouting that nonsense \u2014 seriously, they might be listening\u2026","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":192,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","user":"Yossarian","date":". 11-24-2021, 06:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-25T21:58:52-08:00","id":1468893,"title":"","content":"A very late update today, but a fun one!<br /> <br /> The Tribute Society is one of two social ghoul families in the book. I've tried to have more of those kind of ghoul families, as they didn't really exist in First Edition, and I think it's one of the more interesting concepts that came out of <b>Half-Damned</b>.<br /> <br /> The Tributes are vampire groupies, or vampire stalkers if you're being unkind. They exist just on the edge of the Masquerade, not completely part of the All Night Society, but not wholly apart from it either. They gain Vitae through their mysterious club president, who has...secrets, let's say.<br /> <br /> This is another family that didn't have too many fundamental changes through development. Their benefit was tweaked a bit, but mostly the changes came out of adjusting their backstory. Originally, it was a bit clearer what was really going on, and I felt it was better to leave it more ambiguous; ambiguity is always good for plot hooks! I also beefed up their benefit a bit, which was originally just the tracking ability you'll find in the book. They needed a little more agency, and I think we struck a good balance on that with the final version. I also like to beef up the benefits of social ghoul families, as they lack a lot of the perks of the biological families.<br /> <br /> On a sidenote, unrelated to the text, our usual logo artist wasn't available for this book, so any new symbols for bloodlines and ghoul families you'll see are mine. I was particularly pleased with the Tributes' logo; those teeth came out just about perfectly.<br /> <br /> Before I wrap up, I want to do a little shameless plug. DTRPG is having its Black Friday / Cyber Monday sale. Several of our products are included in that, so now is a great time to check them out if you haven't. In addition, <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/301087/Bloodlines-The-Devoted\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Bloodlines: The Devoted </b>is on sale for a <i>deep </i>discount of $3.99 for Friday only</a>! And, if you already have it, I took this opportunity to implement some errata, both based on comments I've received and just a couple years of hindsight. So, update your files accordingly.<br /> <br /> <b>The Tribute Society: The ones who crave your attention</b><br /> <br /> &quot;I've done everything for you.&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>Where we came from</b><br /> <br /> The Kiss brings euphoria. How could we not want that? Between unrealistic expectations for heteronormative happy endings and puritan cultures that repress our sexualities, there\u2019s massive appeal in the idea of an underworld where unfettered sensuality reigns supreme. Vampires represent everything real life doesn\u2019t: nuance, freedom, and fulfillment. From Christabel to The Giaour, from Carmilla to Dracula, these twisted figures have captivated humanity for generations.<br /> <br /> To we devoted few, they were more than Penny Dreadfuls or opium-fueled poetry. We felt the truth in these tales as others felt the word of God. In 1730, we formed an epistolary club known as the Tribute Society, and we\u2019ve been operating ever since. In the beginning, it was mostly letters exchanged between a few bored vampirophiles, sharing knowledge of the \u201cKindred\u201d and their bloody society. Can\u2019t cross running water. Allergic to garlic. Burned by silver crosses \u2014 we made sure to purge such deterrents from our lives.<br /> <br /> Then we wrote pamphlets, took memberships. By 1893, a woman named Angela Chapman became president of the Society. Known best by the pen name Thalaba, she built many of our organizational and structural supports, but \u2014 more than that \u2014 she got her hands on some genuine blood. The details of this acquisition are somewhat obscure, but however it started, for a fee, you could order a vial of your own and get a little edge in your pursuit. That\u2019s when we Tributes went from observers to active participants.<br /> <br /> Those initiates who reach the rank of the Unveiled are permitted to consume this precious Vitae and become full-fledged members of our little \u201cfamily.\u201d There are three official ranks: Veiled (a newcomer), Unveiled (one who has become a true Tribute), and Bitten (one who has been fed upon by a vampire). Tradition says that each Unveiled member takes on a literary hero or heroine\u2019s name during their acceptance ceremony, as well as a Society-approved surname. After all, if you\u2019re willing to come this far into our little club, you know it isn\u2019t just a hobby: It\u2019s a lifestyle.<br /> <br /> <b>Who we are tonight</b><br /> <br /> Pop culture has always had a vampire in the limelight, and weirdos on the fringes have always been tantalized by the idea of some sexy monster sweeping them off their feet. Vampires \u2014 or so film and literature paint them \u2014 have seen more of the world than any mortal cold fish date ever could, and offer pleasure beyond the wildest imaginings with just a prick of their fangs.<br /> <br /> We Tributes have grown up longing for that bite, believing with all our might that vampires are real. Knowing it. They\u2019re out there, in the shadows, drinking the blood of the living. And, if so, why not our blood? What makes those others so fucking special?<br /> <br /> So, we dive down the rabbit hole of message boards, fan theories, slash fic, and counter-culture sex clubs. We work through endless conspiracies, trying to discern what\u2019s true and what\u2019s trash. The challenge is, with so many \u201cclans,\u201d it\u2019s hard to discern the noise from the signal. All we can do is make educated guesses and hope our digging unearths a real vampire.<br /> <br /> We gather through social media and community centers, and even some progressive churches, sharing our woes with fellow seekers. Sometimes a member shares a lead: a bar purported to be run by a dead man, a location of multiple feedings, photos and paintings of identical faces from across distant decades that must belong to a single individual\u2026 or one of their ghouls. Some of us will drop everything just to chase these threads in the vain hope they\u2019ll bear fruit, exposing ourselves to the dangers of the night for the chance some Dead Prince Charming will decide to take us out for a drink.<br /> <br /> The lucky work our way up the ranks with a patron vampire, but most of us have to do it the hard way. However, if you\u2019ve proven yourself to the organization, Thalaba herself will ship you your own vial of genuine Vitae. There\u2019s a strict regimen recruits need to follow for the \u201cturning\u201d to work: microdoses taken on the hour, consistently, for a month. The change comes over slowly, but you\u2019ll know from the sudden, irrepressible craving for more that you\u2019ve become properly Unveiled.<br /> <br /> For us, once bitten, twice shy is just admitting defeat. That kind of talk\u2019s not for closers. After one rises to the Unveiled rank, the need for a vampire patron escalates. Maybe Kindred can smell the change in us, because it\u2019s easier to attract a Lick\u2019s attention the higher up the ladder you go \u2014 that\u2019s part of the appeal, really. Look hard enough, present yourself on a platter to a blood-sucker, and sooner or later, you\u2019ll get nipped. And the Kiss? It\u2019s everything we dream of and more. A true Tribute will track her first vampire\u2019s every movement, learning everything she can about him, bribing whomever she has to, funneling all her resources into her obsession. She lives, sleeps, and breathes her beloved. Usually she prevails, chumming the water until he can\u2019t resist her. Because if we show them how much we love them, how can they not love us in return?<br /> <br /> <b>Three Seekers (excerpt)</b><br /> <br /> Thalaba Wolfsbane (AKA Angela Chapman), was born in 1871, and it took her thirteen years after beginning her tenure as club president to meet a proper vampire. The tragic Marquise was a Daeva clinging to aristocracy in a world ravaged by the Great War, and she gave Thalaba the idea of creating ranks for her club. Together, they began peddling the Marquise\u2019s Vitae \u2014 willingly, allegedly \u2014 to Thalaba\u2019s most devoted subscribers. Of course, the Marquise\u2019s true role in this is hotly debated among the Tributes, especially after her untimely torpor some hundred years ago. Gossip aside, Thalaba still can\u2019t really explain how the Society\u2019s methods work, like how the Vitae she ships turns her followers into ghouls, or why it doesn\u2019t seem to form a blood bond to\u2026 anyone. The rank and file\u2019s general ignorance of Kindred physiology has helped her dodge more awkward questions, but who even cares? Nothing sinister is going on, according to Thalaba. No one would want a gang of emotionally-stunted snoops keeping constant tabs on vampires. What use would that be?<br /> <br /> <b>Benefit:</b> Ironically, Tributes are true independent ghouls. As long as she has at least a point of Vitae provided by the Society in her system, a Seeker is immune to blood bonds from any vampire she doesn\u2019t have the Swooning Condition toward. However, if she does have the Swooning Condition toward a vampire, she knows where he is at all times, even if he\u2019s Obfuscated. The feeling pulls at her like a compass, firing her addiction for more and giving her laser focus. Unless she has a regnant, a Tribute\u2019s starting Discipline options are Celerity, Majesty, and Vigor.<br /> <br /> <b>Drawback:</b> [REDACTED]<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-25T23:05:52-08:00","id":1468896,"title":"","content":"The Tribute Society looks like nice people. Surely they aren\u2019t suspect of indecent things like manipulating those they \u2018admire.\u2019<br /> <br /> And \u2018social\u2019 ghoul families like that, especially Daeva-ish ones, for some reason make me want to do a Wuxia-style martial arts tradition/school as a ghoul family. Imagine semi-immortal kung-fu ghouls with Vigor and Celerity <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-25T23:30:53-08:00","id":1468901,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1467058-sin-again-daeva-now-available-on-storytellers-vault-2e-requiem-clan-book?p=1468896#post1468896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Tribute Society looks like nice people. Surely they aren\u2019t suspect of indecent things like manipulating those they \u2018admire.\u2019<br /> <br /> And \u2018social\u2019 ghoul families like that, especially Daeva-ish ones, for some reason make me want to do a Wuxia-style martial arts tradition/school as a ghoul family. Imagine semi-immortal kung-fu ghouls with Vigor and Celerity <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Ooo, martial arts school as ghoul family. I\u2019m very into that. Would also fit the Gangrel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-25T23:35:18-08:00","id":1468903,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1467058-sin-again-daeva-now-available-on-storytellers-vault-2e-requiem-clan-book?p=1468901#post1468901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ooo, martial arts school as ghoul family. I\u2019m very into that. Would also fit the Gangrel.</div> </div> </div> </div>Heh, Gangrel-related martial arts ghoul families would look like the martial traditions of \u201cbeyond the border (ie. the Great Wall)\u201d that became tropes and cliches of their own in Korean Wuxia novels.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-26T09:53:14-08:00","id":1468923,"title":"","content":"I really need to read that one... but life got a way to get in my way (that and a Demon the Descent campaign I'm starting to work on as a GM...) but I wanted to say I know the quality will be top notch !","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1233-ur-than","name":"Ur-Than","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-27T19:52:08-08:00","id":1469063,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ur-Than</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1467058-sin-again-daeva-now-available-on-storytellers-vault-2e-requiem-clan-book?p=1468923#post1468923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really need to read that one... but life got a way to get in my way (that and a Demon the Descent campaign I'm starting to work on as a GM...) but I wanted to say I know the quality will be top notch !</div> </div> </div> </div>Always great to hear! I hope you check it out!<br /> <br /> Also, I just realized I forgot to post anything yesterday. That said, we're kind of burning through this one, so I think I'll save our next excerpt for Monday. Then, we'll talk about the Scorned...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-29T13:52:24-08:00","id":1469197,"title":"","content":"A good Monday to you all!<br /> <br /> As promised, let's talk about the Scorned.<br /> <br /> This was one that went through a lot of change in development. The concept didn't change too much (i.e., people who get overwhelmed with Majesty and then can feel nothing but pain), but a lot of the assumptions shifted. Originally, there was a scientific component to their suffering, but I pretty much immediately axed that. One thing I try to do with these books is not to ground supernatural phenomena in the real world, and I felt like making it a tangible neurological disorder made the concept too restrictive, and just felt like a space we weren't equipped to wander into in general. Thus, in the final version, they're entirely supernatural.<br /> <br /> There were also pretty comprehensive mechanics for how to &quot;produce&quot; Scorned. That wasn't a bad impulse, but in the end, decided to leave it for STs to decide. These characters are always going to be Storyteller characters, and I didn't want to have a system that made the Daeva's signature Discipline into a liability. Partially that was a narrative choice, but I don't think there was a very good middle ground to define such a system mechanically. Either it would happen so often that STs would never want to use it, or it would be so rare that the Scorned could never come up in a reasonable way. Even if there was a happy medium, it felt like a bummer to say that, of all the clans, the Daeva have the Discipline that glitches out the worst. I considered making it something Daeva could potentially do on purpose, but that ultimately felt like it was against the theme of the write-up. So, my compromise was no mechanics (though I did leave a suggestion if people really need them). If you want to introduce the Scorned into a player character's plot, go for it, though make sure that's something they'd be into.<br /> <br /> Also: If you've read our other clan books, you may have seen the name &quot;Scorned&quot; before. That's not a coincidence.<br /> <br /> Anyway, let's have a look at the Scorned. Oh, and by the way, since it's Cyber Monday, I thought I'd do a little promotion. If you're interested in the book but haven't picked it up for whatever reason, for the rest of the day, you can get it half off through this link:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?discount=949e43ea1d\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.storytellersvault.com/br...unt=949e43ea1d</a><br /> <br /> As always, if you've enjoyed the book (or any of our work), please consider leaving a star rating or a review! I know I'm a broken record at this point, but it's SO helpful.<br /> <br /> Also, I don't know if this was a problem for anyone, but I finally managed to reduce the size of the file. I don't know why it was so large (I used the same specifications as <b>Ventrue</b>), but now it's a bit more manageable.<br /> <br /> <b>The Scorned: Hell hath no fury<br /> <br /> AKA: Ravagers</b><br /> <br /> &quot;You can't hurt me anymore.&quot;<br /> <br /> Through Majesty, the Daeva do more than enforce reality. They can plum the deepest secrets, sway the unwashed masses, and reap the adoration of fanatical herds. The cruel and uncanny nature of their Discipline perverts a victim\u2019s thoughts and bends their emotions to whatever ends a vampire wishes.<br /> <br /> But emotions aren\u2019t as simple as most Serpents believe. They\u2019re fragile mechanisms tied to a patchwork glob of flesh laughably called a mind. Humans aren\u2019t designed to withstand constant and overwhelming desire.<br /> <br /> In very rare cases, repeated exposure to Majesty can push a mortal to the breaking point. When the fleeting bliss of the vampire\u2019s affection vanishes, the victim realizes in horror that it took every other feeling with it. Suddenly, she no longer feels pleasure in any form. She\u2019s unable to feel anything at all \u2014 except pain. These unfortunates rarely live long, whether taking their own lives or meeting the sharp end of the Masquerade, but a few accept what they\u2019ve become and embrace the only outlet they can. They call themselves the Scorned, and pain is their only pleasure.<br /> <br /> <b>Background</b><br /> <br /> Pain isn\u2019t quite the right word for what Scorned experience, but it\u2019s close enough for government work. Does it feel good? Certainly not. But it does <i>feel</i>, and that\u2019s sufficient. Like wanderers dying of thirst in a desert, Ravagers are willing to experience anything \u2014 no matter how agonizing \u2014 to feel anything at all. This adaptation warps their souls, converting desire to masochism and kindness to sadism. Reborn in agony, Scorned find truth, and in that truth, they find a gospel: Pain must be shared. True joy can only be found in mutual agony. It\u2019s the Golden Rule, after all: Do unto others as you would have them do unto you. So pass that claw hammer; they need to show you how much they care.<br /> <br /> Of course, evangelism is only a side concern. Before the Scorned can bear witness, they must take revenge. Most hunt vampires as a fulltime gig, particularly Kindred of Clan Daeva. A Ravager\u2019s first victim is usually the Lick who ruined him, and if he succeeds (or at least survives), it serves as proof positive that he\u2019s taken back the reins of his life.<br /> <br /> Not all \u201cscorned\u201d humans take up this philosophy. Indeed, in the rare cases where a Daeva ruins her plaything with Majesty, the poor soul usually spends the rest of his short life on copious amounts of anti-depressants, not some revenge quest. True Scorned are rare, but genuine ones always come around to the above belief system. Some Daeva speculate that an outside force must be at play here, or at least that this ideological prevalence is more than coincidence. However, every Ravager who\u2019s been willing to extol her ethos hasn\u2019t said jack about where she got it. To all appearances, it comes to them apropos of nothing, and if that\u2019s the void Majesty opens in the human soul, then the Daeva may have bigger problems coming over the horizon.<br /> <br /> <b>Rumors</b><br /> <br /> <i>\u201cYou can cure them. A colleague of mine knows this Night Doctor who took a series of MRIs of one back in the 90s, and the results suggest physiological repair is possible. Their brains are basically riddled with benign, tumorous growths that act as patches over traumatic brain damage localized in the pleasure centers in the anterior cingulate and prefrontal cortexes. In theory, laparoscopic surgery could break up enough of the tumors to allow for stem cell treatments on the damaged tissue. Of course, being as you can\u2019t even anesthetize them, that would be quite the feat.\u201d</i><br /> <br /> A fabrication, but it\u2019s a story that gets passed around from time to time, tagged with varying degrees of neurological accuracy. No one knows the exact mechanism that breaks Ravagers, and few have gotten close enough to find out. Yet the question remains: Can they be cured? Yes, but it\u2019s not something any vampire is going to be down for. The taste of Vitae invigorates the Scorned, offering emotional clarity if consumed in mass quantities. A Ravager is created when a vampire breaks her heart, but all it takes to fix her is returning the favor. If one of them consumes a torpid vampire\u2019s heart, the damage to her soul begins to mend. This healing process isn\u2019t instantaneous, but it\u2019s the only known path to recovery.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":192,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","user":"Yossarian","date":". 11-29-2021, 08:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-30T15:20:39-08:00","id":1469274,"title":"","content":"Hello again! We're fast approaching the end of previews from Chapter Four, so let's have a look at the final ghoul family: The Histrions.<br /> <br /> This was a really fun concept from start to finish, and lays on the comedy a little more than we usual do (if in a rather dark way). I wanted a more humorous tone with this book -- not &quot;lighter,&quot; but sassier, as befits the clan. The Histrions fit that well, with their carefully constructed self-delusions, and, similar to the Tribute Society, serve as something of a funhouse mirror to certain aspects of the Daeva.<br /> <br /> Development for this one was pretty straightforward. The only big mechanical change was giving them easier access to Majesty; as I said above, I try to give the social families a little more oomph, and considering what the Histrions are <i>really </i>for, it felt like fair compensation.<br /> <br /> Tomorrow, I'll do an excerpt from VLAD, the &quot;little problem&quot; of the Damned (and, appropriately, the very last thing in the book). After that, I might excerpt some stuff from chapter three, including what we've got on the Daeva bane, but I think I'll be done with excerpts at that point. Stick around, though, as I might have a little treat for everyone who's been following this thread soon...<br /> <br /> Histrion: The ones who perform<br /> <br /> &quot;But\u2026 what if I\u2019m no hero? It might hurt you if you got to know me.&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>Where we came from</b><br /> <br /> The Histrions emerged in Rome\u2019s wake, as the Lancea et Sanctum\u2019s Traditions became Kindred law. For Christianity to outlast the Empire, it needed exemplars, and if the Twelve Apostles couldn\u2019t do it, propaganda would work in a pinch. The first Histrions (literally, \u201cactors\u201d) were drawn from circus troupes and other entertainers, selected for their talents in holding a crowd\u2019s attention. With morality plays and other didactic theater, the dead Church would show the kine how to live up to Christ\u2019s standards, then \u201cquiz\u201d them on their piety. The regnants of these ghouls were mostly Daeva, ones who understood the dividends of high production values even when it comes to faith. They also recognized that their illiterate flocks couldn\u2019t be tested if they didn\u2019t know the rules, and so the Histrions went about making them crystal clear.<br /> <br /> Those Shepherds who brought the most souls to the Lord were blessed with Vitae and power. Actors were often viewed as beyond redemption in these times \u2014 little better than whores and thieves \u2014 so the Sanctified had few qualms about damning their messengers even as they let them guide the masses to the light. The Gospel from a sinner\u2019s mouth is still the Gospel, and a reprobate is far easier for a vampire to control than a saint.<br /> <br /> Perhaps that was the problem. As successful Histrions lived it up in the lap of luxury, they began to resemble their dead masters, and not just figuratively. The more they were rewarded, the paler their skin became, and the more depraved their decadent tastes. They say imitation is the sincerest form of flattery, and if so, these ghouls were exemplary sycophants. Eventually, little difference remained between the monsters and their servants.<br /> <br /> The name of the first assassinated Histrion is lost, but later written accounts claim it was an ignoble end. During the final performance of a shockingly sexual production of <i>Ordo Virtutum</i>, an audience member stormed the stage and gutted the player portraying Chastity. The assailant proclaimed he\u2019d slain an agent of Hell and urged the crowd to cleanse the remaining taint. A riot ensued.<br /> <br /> This was not to be an isolated incident. The Serpents behind this endeavor became laughingstocks, myopic fools who\u2019d created a bunch of narcissists in their own image. The project was dead.<br /> However, an actor can never leave the stage until the curtain call. As more of these ghouls fell to violent \u201cfans,\u201d the Serpents saw a brand new angle. Maybe their Shepherds couldn\u2019t make anyone keep the faith, but they sure could provide cover. After all, the difference between a real vampire and a patsy who\u2019s groomed to act like one is academic to the man with the stake. Eventually, these Daeva would turn their blunder into an asset, and even tonight, the Histrions play on. They just don\u2019t realize who their real audience is.<br /> <br /> <b>Who we are tonight</b><br /> <br /> Histrions are designer ghouls, bespoke insurance policies for paranoid corpses. Modern Shepherds are ethereal beauties with melancholic, pale complexions, subtly guided into filling all the various stereotypes pop culture has bestowed on the living dead. Some Patsies are even altered physically, made to look similar to their regnants or otherwise enhanced to fit certain aesthetic markers. Not understanding the Kindred condition, some are even tricked into believing they are vampires. Histrions are blessed with good looks, resources, and even new passions. The cost, of course, is that nearly all of them wind up dead.<br /> <br /> Placed in large social environs, their unique traits draw both positive and negative attention, luring out stalkers, aspiring hunters, and other undesirables without risking a vampire\u2019s Masquerade or Requiem. By pampering the ghoul and building up her ego, putting her in positions of vague authority becomes a layer of protection. Suddenly all the vampire\u2019s bank accounts are in her name, and all the records list her home address. The entire purpose of a Histrion is to act alone upon the stage, and compared to the eternal servitude of other ghouls, this can be quite a blessing. And if their lives end tragically as they take a firebomb meant for someone else? Well, then they\u2019ve performed very well indeed.<br /> <br /> Most Shepherds fulfill this duty within a few years. Fueled by the ceaseless power fantasies seeded by her regnant, a Histrion rarely realizes she\u2019s a designated meat shield \u2014 after all, how could creatures as generous and powerful as the Kindred allow such cruelty? Up to the moment she takes silver blade to the throat, a Shepherd is a pampered, beloved lapdog, and even in dire straits, she\u2019ll play her part to the hilt. She\u2019s special, dammit. No human can dodge a bullet, but a Histrion just might try.<br /> <br /> That doesn\u2019t mean Patsies never piece together their morbid purpose, especially if they survive one of these misguided assassinations. What was once delight in their power turns to ash, and when the ghoul tries to confront her regnant, she\u2019s either struck down for outliving her purpose or cowed by the seductive words of a slave master. Or maybe the event is just tossed in the memory hole, and she\u2019s left to wonder where she got these burns. In any case, many Players wind up justifying these attacks as happenstance, or come to believe their regnants really didn\u2019t know.<br /> <br /> Ultimately, Histrion lives are brief fireworks in an endless night, pretty sparks designed to fizzle away and be forgotten. Just more noise for the Cacophony.<br /> <br /> <b>Benefit:</b> The Histrions exude a natural receptiveness, making them alluring as lovers, confidants, and decoys. All Players gain Striking Looks 1 (or an Experience if they already have it) and begin play with an extra Discipline dot in Majesty. In addition, they lose a touch of color in their skin and a bit of volume in their heartbeats, enjoying a +3 on any Expression, Persuasion, or Subterfuge rolls to convince uninitiated mortals (intentionally or not) that they\u2019re \u201cvampires.\u201d<br /> <br /> <b>Drawback:</b> [REDACTED]<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-01T13:13:20-08:00","id":1469352,"title":"","content":"Have you talked to your doctor about VLAD?<br /> <br /> VLAD continues our tradition of including vampire diseases in these books (cf., Malkavia and the Noctuku Strain). I don't <i>think </i>any of my authors has a Gangrel disease planned for the next book, but we shall have to wait and see.<br /> <br /> VLAD is our not-so-subtle joke about vampire performance anxiety, though it's got its roots back in the World of Darkness. It's partly a CofD take on the Withering effect from <b>Gehenna</b> (hence the nickname), which was a cool concept, but was very limited to the apocalyptic metaplot of the Revised Edition, so I was happy to see this variation on that theme.<br /> <br /> What I particularly like about the write-up is the backstory involving the disease's discoverer; it provides a little more meat for the Storyteller to build a narrative around. The disease itself isn't that complicated, so the details about Dr. Heinrich provide an inherent hook to the concept that goes beyond just inflicting it on characters. It also means the rumors and story seeds could have some connective tissue, as it were. Things like VLAD are ultimately just plot hooks with mechanics, so I really like that this one has so many angles to it.<br /> <br /> From a broader view, one of my desires for the antagonists/allies chapter was to keep the write-ups a bit tighter. With the exception of the Flowers, Alu, and Nemites, I wanted to keep things pretty strictly to three pages each, because that meant we could fit more content in without bloating the book excessively. Things like Solace and VLAD were really helpful for that: they're simple, fun concepts with relatively light mechanics.<br /> <br /> Anyway, enjoy the except. And with that, we're done with my dev notes! I hope you enjoyed the ride. I <i>might </i>be back with something about the Daeva curse write-up in the third chapter, but it's a little hard to preview it without just posting the whole thing. I also could use a little break from writing these up; as fun as they are, it does take up a good chunk of my time, and the Gangrel book isn't going to develop itself.<br /> <br /> That said, I'm happy to open this thread up to questions (even if it's just &quot;How does this Devotion work?&quot;) So, if you have any thoughts or comments or queries, sound off below.<br /> <br /> Also, I promised a little treat above, so watch out for that on Friday.<br /> <br /> ALSO, please drop us some reviews! It's always an uphill battle getting them, but I good review (or just a good star-rating) can really help people get past the barrier of buying community content.<br /> <br /> <b>VLAD: Our little problem</b><br /> <br /> &quot;This has never happened to me before!&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>AKA: The Withering, KED</b><br /> <br /> Sometimes stress, anxiety, and life in general mess with your head. The quagmire of living in this world can lead to\u2026 things\u2026 just not working the way they should. It\u2019s a natural part of the aging process, and it happens to everyone eventually.<br /> <br /> Performance issues aren\u2019t limited to the bedroom, either. Everyone from professional athletics to chess masters knows about the yips and the twisties. Sometimes you just choke. There isn\u2019t a person alive who hasn\u2019t experienced a bout of strange and sudden discombobulation, or just random incompetence related to something they\u2019re good at. It\u2019s all part of being alive \u2014 though even that isn\u2019t a given.<br /> <br /> A strange disease has arisen among the Kindred population known as Vampiric Labile Abnormality Disorder (VLAD). Those suffering from the disease find themselves increasingly unable to use their innate abilities: Calling on Disciplines turns into a crapshoot, lashing out becomes arduous, and eventually, even the Kiss doesn\u2019t work.<br /> <br /> <b>Background</b><br /> <br /> If it\u2019s hard enough to diagnose conditions that only affect a small segment of the human population, and diagnosing creatures as aloof and paranoid as Kindred is nigh impossible. Most vampires refuse to share details of their psychology with anyone, lest they reveal a weakness to their rivals, and even those who are open about such things have little recourse. Sure, there\u2019s always that one Mekhet who attends weird support groups after hours, or who turns their analyst into a ghoul, but these solutions are short term at best. Maybe that\u2019s why VLAD wasn\u2019t properly identified until 2009.<br /> <br /> When Dr. Andrea Heinrich finished her PhD in psychology from Stanford, she was Embraced within a week. Her sire, Maximilian, was an Invictus magnate who wanted to turn her education to his own ends, modernizing his company\u2019s glitzy ad campaigns to keep consumers ignorant of the vampire selling to them. It was demeaning, demoralizing work, but Andrea had little choice. Max was an intimidating, tyrannical, seemingly all-powerful elder \u2014 until one night, he wasn\u2019t.<br /> <br /> Max\u2019s Disciplines first failed him at a First Estate soir\u00e9e during an attempt to victimize a ghoul. Instead of being cowed, the unphased minion shot back a humiliating retort that filled the gathering with mocking laughter, directed at the near-frenzied Max. From there, his condition continued to decline until he was reduced to hiding away in his haven and feeding from blood bags his servants stole from the hospital.<br /> <br /> Max needed help, and Andrea was happy to get back to her roots. After months of grueling therapy and study, she developed a treatment plan that incorporated clinical behaviorism, exposure therapy, and a hefty dose of Dominate. And it worked: Max was cured. Of course, in his desperation, he\u2019d allowed himself to be blood bound to his childe, and she wasn\u2019t above slipping in a few self-serving mental triggers and memory alterations.<br /> <br /> With her sire\u2019s fortune at her disposal, Andrea has created a foundation for extra-normal research, and its first focus is her sire\u2019s former disorder. It was Dr. Heinrich who came up with the acronym, though she was tempted to name it after Max.<br /> <br /> <b>Infection</b><br /> <br /> VLAD is as much virus as psychological disorder. Bizarrely, it doesn\u2019t pass through any physical means, though it appears in a Kindred victim\u2019s blood like any other pathogen. The disease instead spreads when a vampire witnesses a carrier strike out using one of her Disciplines, or any other deathly power.<br /> While it doesn\u2019t move through shared vectors like Vitae, it does have an easier time passing among vampires who share blood ties. Kindred of the same clan have a much better chance of catching it from each other, and the closer one\u2019s relation to another vampire, the more difficult it is to resist<br /> <br /> <b>Systems</b><br /> <br /> Whenever a vampire witnesses another bloodsucker exhibit an obvious symptom of VLAD, such as failing a Discipline or flubbing his Predatory Aura, she must roll Resolve + Composure minus her own Blood Potency. On a failure, she gains the Shaken Condition, fearful that something like that could happen to her. This roll is further penalized by her degree of Blood Sympathy to the other vampire (<b>Vampire</b>, p. 98), but takes a +3 if the characters are of different clans. If the vampire suffers a failure on any Discipline or attempt to lash out before she resolves Shaken, it becomes the VLAD (Stage One) Condition.<br /> <br /> <b>VLAD (Persistent)</b><br /> <br /> [REDACTED]<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-01T14:30:43-08:00","id":1469358,"title":"","content":"Briefly reacquiring conscious thought after last month reduced me to a puddle of unthinking goo so I can say that I had so much fun doing art for this book! In particular, the Histrions and VLAD were a joy to illustrate, though the Flowers might be my favorite piece I contributed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Posting gives me anxiety, but I'm still happy to be here</i><br /> Habitual Lurker, Vengrel Liker, Acolyte Apologist, She/Her","edited":{"userid":25955,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25955-somethingfishy","user":"SomethingFishy","date":".  Fixed a typo. Higher thought is still not quite there, I guess. 12-01-2021, 05:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25955-somethingfishy","name":"SomethingFishy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25955_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-01T16:18:33-08:00","id":1469369,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SomethingFishy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1467058-sin-again-daeva-now-available-on-storytellers-vault-2e-requiem-clan-book?p=1469358#post1469358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Briefly reacquiring conscious thought after last month reduced me to a puddle of unthinking goo so I can say that I had so much fun doing art for this book! In particular, the Histrions and VLAD were a joy to illustrate, though the Flowers might be my favorite piece I contributed.</div> </div> </div> </div>The illustration for VLAD really brings the whole thing together, honestly.<br /> <br /> Fish did all the illustrations for Chapter Four, so if you like those, you can send your praise her way! My personal favourite is the Children of Nirriti illustration, because it <i>really </i>captures the spirit of our new version.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-03T14:53:33-08:00","id":1469531,"title":"","content":"Alright, I promised a little treat for Friday, so here it is!<br /> <br /> Disclaimer: This isn't really done, in the sense that nothing I do is ever done until forces conspire to make me stop. That is, I'll be tweaking it for a while yet, but I wanted to do the title reveal with the cover (even though I'm pretty sure I spoiled the title before!)<br /> <br /> Coming soon...<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://i.ibb.co/YdzC0zM/untitled.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-03T16:13:51-08:00","id":1469539,"title":"","content":"The Wild Hunt. Ooh. Wonder if we\u2019d get some ghostly and fae motifs added to the usual bestial &amp; therianthropic motifs of the Gangrels.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-17T20:47:39-08:00","id":1470764,"title":"","content":"Hey all, just popping in to let you know that from now until end of day December 31st, we're offering a big discounted bundle of all our Vampire books! If you haven't had a chance to pick these up, or want to complete your collection, now's a great time!<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/381051/2021-All-Night-Society-Sale-BUNDLE?affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">2021 All Night Society Bundle</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":192,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","user":"Yossarian","date":". 12-17-2021, 11:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-31T20:44:22-07:00","id":1477824,"title":"","content":"Yossarian<br /> Two questions: in the Blowout system I am confused by one mechanic. The Exceptional Success for the desperation action says that no desperation action took place. Aside from the direct contradiction it makes me think that you get the same result if you solve all the hurdles beforehand. The difference in extra scenes is not a trivial one. I tried looking in both the pdf and here for a clue either way but found no elaboration. Could you clarify? Does solving all hurdles give an option between an extra scene or regaining the 10-again for stalled tilts?<br /> <br /> Another thing. How is your progress with the Gangrel? Percentage of completion? Approximate time to release?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26112-excess","name":"Excess","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-31T22:12:56-07:00","id":1477831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Excess</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1467058-sin-again-daeva-now-available-on-storytellers-vault-2e-requiem-clan-book?p=1477824#post1477824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yossarian<br /> Two questions: in the Blowout system I am confused by one mechanic. The Exceptional Success for the desperation action says that no desperation action took place. Aside from the direct contradiction it makes me think that you get the same result if you solve all the hurdles beforehand. The difference in extra scenes is not a trivial one. I tried looking in both the pdf and here for a clue either way but found no elaboration. Could you clarify? Does solving all hurdles give an option between an extra scene or regaining the 10-again for stalled tilts?<br /> <br /> Another thing. How is your progress with the Gangrel? Percentage of completion? Approximate time to release?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Resolution Results are for the Tilt altogether, not the desperation action (though I see why you'd think that, because it's written rather vaguely). If you manage to clear all of the Hurdles without taking a desperation action, it's an exceptional success, whereas it's always a normal success if you manage to eke things out with a desperation roll. There isn't a specific exceptional success result for the desperation role, which <i>is </i>a little confusing, because a dramatic failure is the same as the overall Resolution one. Long story short, what's written is a bit muddy, so I'll make sure to address that in an update, probably whenever Gangrel comes out (there are a lot of updates coming...)<br /> <br /> Speaking of Gangrel, I'm hoping late this month or early next! Still waiting on some final things, but it's imminent!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-31T22:45:56-07:00","id":1477833,"title":"","content":"Just because this is a fairly simple fix, here's the rewrite. Does this make things a bit clearer?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If all hurdles are overcome after each character acted, the Tilt is resolved with an exceptional success. However, if any hurdles remain, the coterie must make an act of desperation. To do so, the players elect a point character to attempt a final, heroic effort. Her player describes a Hail Mary action and then makes a roll penalized by the number of remaining hurdles, plus any other modifiers. This action uses a different Attribute + Skill than the one she used before, as something needs to fundamentally change about the character\u2019s tactics. The number of remaining hurdles should influence the narrative complexity of this effort.<br /> Succeed or fail, the character refreshes a Willpower for taking this action. The results of this roll are only pass or fail, but the troupe can choose to make a regular failure a dramatic one if the choice is unanimous.<br /> Tilt Resolution Results<br /> Success: All hurdles have been removed, but the coterie had to resort to desperation to do so. The Tilt ends and each coterie member gains a Beat for contributing. A scene passes.<br /> Exceptional Success: The coterie cleared all hurdles without a desperation action, and the issue was handled so efficiently that they have time to spare. Choose one: Don\u2019t lose a scene or regain the 10-again quality on a stalled Tilt.<br /> Failure: The coterie left hurdles in place; the Tilt continues to wreak havoc and a scene passes. The team must begin from scratch on another attempt later in the evening. If the coterie has can\u2019t stall any further scenes, the Blowout is also a failure.<br /> Dramatic Failure: The coterie resolved no hurdles or chose to dramatically fail the desperation action. As with a failure, but the Tilt gains an additional hurdle for later. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":192,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","user":"Yossarian","date":". 04-01-2022, 02:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-05T01:32:14-07:00","id":1478040,"title":"","content":"I have issues that can keep me from responding a long while. So forgive the few days this took.<br /> <br /> I would have quoted you here to make my point easier, but I don't know how to quote a quote. (I will understand if you don't want to do any more editing, I have a mind for little errors)<br /> <br /> Anyways Yossarian, yes, it is clearer, but I still see some issues. Three errors here and a question. <br /> <br /> The &quot;failure&quot; outcome has one too many &quot;has&quot;.<br /> <br /> You describe the roll as &quot;only pass or fail&quot;, but four outcomes isn't binary.<br /> <br /> You still simultaneously say that having hurdles remain means that a desperation must happen and yet doesn't have to.<br /> <br /> Despite all that you still make it clearer because I no longer doubt what Exceptional Successes can do.<br /> <br /> My question is on the &quot;Hail Mary&quot;. Is it the official name for the mechanic and &quot;desperation action&quot; just means the Hail Mary had less than an Exceptional Success? <br /> <br /> I also reread the Blowout mechanics. I was trying to see if your changes here caused a contradiction elsewhere, thankfully that wasn't hard. You kept the mechanics nearly entirely contained in one small part of the book. It is not like this is a mechanic's guide to cars or anything. <br /> <br /> The closest thing to a contradiction I found was that your example story with the &quot;joyless (Nosferatu) asshole&quot; tilt referenced desperation actions and I still don't know if you changed the name. I am fairly sure you didn't. <br /> <br /> Also, on page 81 section &quot;Hosting&quot;, you have an incomplete sentence. &quot;Hosting is the night of.&quot;<br /> <br /> Finally, if you put that section in the book as is the readers likely won't have the context of our conversation. They will likely guess that the &quot;Exceptional Success&quot; of clearing all hurdles is the same as for desperation actions, but you could remove that momentary confusion. <br /> <br /> I really do have a mind for little errors. That is why I don't expect them all to be corrected, in anything I critique.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26112-excess","name":"Excess","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-05T03:59:19-07:00","id":1478047,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Excess</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1467058-sin-again-daeva-now-available-on-storytellers-vault-2e-requiem-clan-book?p=1478040#post1478040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have issues that can keep me from responding a long while. So forgive the few days this took.<br /> <br /> I would have quoted you here to make my point easier, but I don't know how to quote a quote. (I will understand if you don't want to do any more editing, I have a mind for little errors)<br /> <br /> Anyways Yossarian, yes, it is clearer, but I still see some issues. Three errors here and a question. <br /> <br /> The &quot;failure&quot; outcome has one too many &quot;has&quot;.<br /> <br /> You describe the roll as &quot;only pass or fail&quot;, but four outcomes isn't binary.<br /> <br /> You still simultaneously say that having hurdles remain means that a desperation must happen and yet doesn't have to.<br /> <br /> Despite all that you still make it clearer because I no longer doubt what Exceptional Successes can do.<br /> <br /> My question is on the &quot;Hail Mary&quot;. Is it the official name for the mechanic and &quot;desperation action&quot; just means the Hail Mary had less than an Exceptional Success? <br /> <br /> I also reread the Blowout mechanics. I was trying to see if your changes here caused a contradiction elsewhere, thankfully that wasn't hard. You kept the mechanics nearly entirely contained in one small part of the book. It is not like this is a mechanic's guide to cars or anything. <br /> <br /> The closest thing to a contradiction I found was that your example story with the &quot;joyless (Nosferatu) asshole&quot; tilt referenced desperation actions and I still don't know if you changed the name. I am fairly sure you didn't. <br /> <br /> Also, on page 81 section &quot;Hosting&quot;, you have an incomplete sentence. &quot;Hosting is the night of.&quot;<br /> <br /> Finally, if you put that section in the book as is the readers likely won't have the context of our conversation. They will likely guess that the &quot;Exceptional Success&quot; of clearing all hurdles is the same as for desperation actions, but you could remove that momentary confusion. <br /> <br /> I really do have a mind for little errors. That is why I don't expect them all to be corrected, in anything I critique.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for pointing out the typos (\u201cnight of\u201d isn\u2019t one, though; it\u2019s just an idiom). Hail Mary was my way of trying not to use the word desperation eight billion times in a single paragraph; however, capitalized words in White Wolf books are always dodgy, so better to go with clarity over style in this case. TL;DR, it\u2019s not a name change.<br /> <br /> From your response, I think I just need to rewrite the section. The distinction between the results of the desperation roll and the results of the Tilt overall is too confusing.<br /> <br /> In the meantime, for clarity sake, here\u2019s how it\u2019s supposed to work:<br /> <br /> If the players clear all hurdles in the allotted turns, clearing the Tilt is an exceptional success.<br /> <br /> If the players don\u2019t clear all hurdles in the allotted turns, they must make a desperation roll, mandatorily, no other option. If that desperation roll succeeds, the Tilt is a normal success, as listed. If it fails, the Tilt fails. This individual dice roll is only pass or fail, but the players can choose to dramatically fail it. If the player rolls an exceptional success on the desperation roll, it would only be a regular success for the Tilt. I think that\u2019s the source of your confusion: the exceptional success is for clearing all hurdles without desperation; it\u2019s <i>not</i> what happens if you roll five successes on the desperation roll.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I really do appreciate the feedback! I\u2019ll make sure all of that is communicated better in the update.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-09T08:46:36-07:00","id":1478367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1467058-sin-again-daeva-now-available-on-storytellers-vault-2e-requiem-clan-book?p=1478047#post1478047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thanks for pointing out the typos (\u201cnight of\u201d isn\u2019t one, though; it\u2019s just an idiom). Hail Mary was my way of trying not to use the word desperation eight billion times in a single paragraph; however, capitalized words in White Wolf books are always dodgy, so better to go with clarity over style in this case. TL;DR, it\u2019s not a name change.<br /> <br /> From your response, I think I just need to rewrite the section. The distinction between the results of the desperation roll and the results of the Tilt overall is too confusing.<br /> <br /> In the meantime, for clarity sake, here\u2019s how it\u2019s supposed to work:<br /> <br /> If the players clear all hurdles in the allotted turns, clearing the Tilt is an exceptional success.<br /> <br /> If the players don\u2019t clear all hurdles in the allotted turns, they must make a desperation roll, mandatorily, no other option. If that desperation roll succeeds, the Tilt is a normal success, as listed. If it fails, the Tilt fails. This individual dice roll is only pass or fail, but the players can choose to dramatically fail it. If the player rolls an exceptional success on the desperation roll, it would only be a regular success for the Tilt. I think that\u2019s the source of your confusion: the exceptional success is for clearing all hurdles without desperation; it\u2019s <i>not</i> what happens if you roll five successes on the desperation roll.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I really do appreciate the feedback! I\u2019ll make sure all of that is communicated better in the update.</div> </div> </div> </div>Three outcomes (dramatic failure) still is not a binary, otherwise, you are now making more sense about this than ever.<br /> <br /> One other thing. I asked about the Gangrel book earlier. If you merely said you declined to give an approximate due date then fine, but not answering at all is annoying. It really doesn't matter because it will be out eventually and you will have my money.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26112-excess","name":"Excess","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-09T08:50:40-07:00","id":1478368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Excess</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1467058-sin-again-daeva-now-available-on-storytellers-vault-2e-requiem-clan-book?p=1478367#post1478367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One other thing. I asked about the Gangrel book earlier. If you merely said you declined to give an approximate due date then fine, but not answering at all is annoying.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's also annoying and extremely rude to ignore an answer and then call someone annoying for not giving you something they gave you:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1467058-sin-again-daeva-now-available-on-storytellers-vault-2e-requiem-clan-book?p=1477831#post1477831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking of Gangrel, I'm hoping late this month or early next! Still waiting on some final things, but it's imminent!</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-24T06:00:05-07:00","id":1479417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1467058-sin-again-daeva-now-available-on-storytellers-vault-2e-requiem-clan-book?p=1478368#post1478368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's also annoying and extremely rude to ignore an answer and then call someone annoying for not giving you something they gave you:<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Didn't notice that. My bad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26112-excess","name":"Excess","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-24T06:08:11-07:00","id":1479418,"title":"","content":"Last thing Yossarian: I couldn't find the &quot;night of&quot; idiom on the internet. I read long lists of idioms that contained the word &quot;night&quot;, even if only in the examples of said idioms. Couldn't find that one, so I literally don't know what it means. Even if you tell me I can't corroborate you. Truth be told I am just about done with editing &quot;sin again&quot;. If you ignore it, I will ignore it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26112-excess","name":"Excess","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-25T11:38:50-07:00","id":1479496,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Excess</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1467058-sin-again-daeva-now-available-on-storytellers-vault-2e-requiem-clan-book?p=1479418#post1479418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Last thing Yossarian: I couldn't find the &quot;night of&quot; idiom on the internet.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://ell.stackexchange.com/questions/134041/the-night-of-common-phrase-or-just-the-night-of-something\" target=\"_blank\">https://ell.stackexchange.com/questi...t-of-something</a><br /> Refer to Jacob C's answer.<br /> <br /> Also, Laurel's answer here:<br /> <a href=\"https://english.stackexchange.com/questions/538242/origin-and-usage-of-day-of\" target=\"_blank\">https://english.stackex