kness/vampire-the-requiem/1467058-sin-again-daeva-now-available-on-storytellers-vault-2e-requiem-clan-book?p=1482035#post1482035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The irony, again, is that it's an anime property I don't like, but boy was it a great metaphor for what I wanted out of Vigor powers. I promise I'm not a total curmudgeon about Japanese cartoons...</div> </div> </div> </div>Curiously I'm kind of a curmudgeon with Anime, but I really like One Punch Man! But then, irony is the name of its game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-26T21:04:50-07:00","id":1482054,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1467058-sin-again-daeva-now-available-on-storytellers-vault-2e-requiem-clan-book?p=1482035#post1482035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The irony, again, is that it's an anime property I don't like, but boy was it a great metaphor for what I wanted out of Vigor powers. I promise I'm not a total curmudgeon about Japanese cartoons...<br /> <br /> EDIT: Oops, posted the Gangrel excerpt in the wrong thread! It's in the correct one now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yeah, no, I get it. Actual curmudgeons about the Japanese cartoons self-identify as anime fans, for starters, and make no apologies for not liking most everything except their niche favorites. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-29T02:39:21-07:00","id":1482231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1467058-sin-again-daeva-now-available-on-storytellers-vault-2e-requiem-clan-book?p=1479496#post1479496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;https://ell.stackexchange.com/questions/134041/the-night-of-common-phrase-or-just-the-night-of-something&amp;quot;\" target=\"_blank\">https://ell.stackexchange.com/questi...t-of-something</a><br /> Refer to Jacob C's answer.<br /> <br /> Also, Laurel's answer here:<br /> <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;https://english.stackexchange.com/questions/538242/origin-and-usage-of-day-of&amp;quot;\" target=\"_blank\">https://english.stackexchange.com/qu...sage-of-day-of</a><br /> <br /> <br /> Sorry, are you the editor of this product or something?</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for finding a source for me. A cursory look resembles an English class though.<br /> <br /> As for your question: what are you talking about? What do you mean &quot;the&quot; editor? The forums are completely free to public perusal, so having an account is primarily about interaction with the creative process. It took some time in my conversation with Yossarian to make sure we understood each other, but Yossarian didn't treat my feedback as presumptuous. The official books are not that different. In some cases the developers sell a digital copy in need of editing to the fanbase who then fill an online form detailing found errors. In other words they sometimes literally sell the position of editor to hundreds at least, including me. I imagine they must have some final editor that decides what to do with our suggestions. In other words, I am just another content creator that gives and receives feedback with other creators, and am not the least bit special for it. I expected Yossarian to appreciate my help like I appreciate yours, and if he disagreed with my suggestions I would accept that it is his thread and therefore his rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26112-excess","name":"Excess","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-29T05:54:48-07:00","id":1482245,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Excess</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1467058-sin-again-daeva-now-available-on-storytellers-vault-2e-requiem-clan-book?p=1482231#post1482231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for your question: what are you talking about? What do you mean &quot;the&quot; editor?</div> </div> </div> </div>Most people pointing out typos in this manner do not refer to it as &quot;editing&quot; a book they do not have write-access to or a formal role as a proofreader or copy-editor on, because it suggests that what they are doing is their job rather than a very minor favor that doesn't warrant drawing attention to their own role.<br /> <br /> You are not editing the book; you are a random stranger on the internet pointing out (and sometimes erroneously, at that) typographical errors in a piece of fan-content for the developer to correct, and according that act a term more specialized than the descriptive and announcing to the forums that you're &quot;just about done&quot; with this minor act of piecemeal volunteer proofreading does, in fact, sound incredibly presumptuous, especially taken in combination with (and immediately following) you giving a very off-the-cuff apology for calling someone annoying because you didn't notice that they answered a question you asked clearly and promptly.<br /> <br /> I sometimes spend hours or days of my time combing through the pre-errata copies of official books so I can submit typos and errors to the errata forms Onyx Path puts out with them. I don't refer to that process as &quot;editing&quot; or announce when I'm &quot;just about done&quot; with the process, because I am not an editor and I have no reason to expect anybody on the forums to care that I think I've finished a personal process that wasn't important enough to say I started in the first place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 05-29-2022, 09:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-29T12:13:26-07:00","id":1482277,"title":"","content":"Could we just drop this line of discussion? As much as I do appreciate feedback, I'm not collecting errata (that's not really what the thread was for), and I'm not interested in having this back and forth keep sporadically spilling into my inbox. I'm more than happy to answer questions about the book, of course, especially if something isn't clear.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new